lanned or in_progress where significant gaps remain, I'll structure predictions around what median tier interpretation would suggest for the consolidated findings. For the data-rich ones like pi05, I'll summarize the predicted interpretation rather than enumerate individual sub-experiments.\n\nNow looking at the remaining experiments: libero suite expansion needs cross-suite predictions, VTR on non-Object suites has partial data that suggests certain performance patterns, OpenVLA shows zero success on VTR with only VTC in progress, OpenVLA M-sweep encountered training failures, OFT is blocked by GPU compatibility issues, RoboFlamingo training was terminated, and there are pending CV measurements and threshold localization experiments to account for.\n\nI'm now compiling the comprehensive YAML predictions with detailed rationale. The median tier assumes more conservative improvements—axis-2 amplification between 10-25 percentage points, CV scaling correlations in the 0.6-0.85 range, cross-suite accuracy around 75-90%, and VTR recovery ratios near 0.9-1.0. I'm grounding these predictions in the substantial existing dataset to ensure consistency across all the experimental variants.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":179,"cache_read_input_tokens":130289,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":179},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f3a93c25-07a2-42fa-8e9c-436d384627d6","uuid":"ff563dcf-4876-438b-bf5f-7f69ef61750f"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_017oH5bAYnMmFSMgDcXA8myA","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now I have the full experiment plan and the extensive registry data. Let me generate the median tier predictions.\n\n```yaml\ntier: median\nnarrative_guidance: >\n  2-axis framework directionally correct but需要 qualify 2-3 个 edge cases。\n  Claim 1 弱化为 'primarily explained by connector architecture, with task complexity as a modulating factor'。\n  Claim 5 加限定 'at moderate compression (k=0.5-0.7)'，k=0.3 reversal 移入 Discussion。\n  VTR 明确为 pixel-shuffle-specific solution。Paper identity 从 'analysis + method' 调整为 'primarily analysis with targeted method for worst-case architecture'。\n  Title 改为更保守的 'How Vision Connectors Shape Token Pruning Robustness in VLAs'。\n  仍提交 CoRL，contribution statement 聚焦 diagnostic insight。\n\nimagined_experiments:\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # 1. π0.5 Cross-Suite Immune Confirmation (plan_id: c1_pi05_immune_confirmation)\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"π0.5 4-Suite Pruning Characterization — Median Tier Consolidation\"\n    plan_id: c1_pi05_immune_confirmation\n    description: >\n      π0.5 (4B, PaliGemma linear proj, CV=0.055) 在 4 个 LIBERO suites 的 pruning response。\n      Median tier 预测：Object 上 random cliff (k=0.85-0.925) 是 Object-specific 而非 universal；\n      Goal/Long 上 Axis-2 amplification 弱于 X-VLA (<15pp for π0.5 vs 27.8pp for X-VLA)。\n      CV scaling law 在 k=0.5 成立但 k=0.3 reversal 需要限定讨论。\n    expected_results:\n      # Baselines (confirmed)\n      pi05_baseline_object: 98.2\n      pi05_baseline_spatial: 97.2\n      pi05_baseline_goal: 96.4\n      pi05_baseline_long: 92.8\n      pi05_cv: 0.055\n\n      # Object suite — random cliff confirmed Object-specific\n      pi05_random_k095_object_sr: 72.5  # mean of 74.0/71.1/72.8\n      pi05_random_k0925_object_sr: 28.8  # mean of 27.6/30.0\n      pi05_random_k09_object_sr: 10.2   # mean of 9.0/10.8/9.6\n      pi05_random_k085_object_sr: 4.4    # mean of 5.0/3.8/4.4\n      pi05_random_k07_object_sr: 75.5    # mean of 77.2/73.8/74.0\n      pi05_random_k05_object_sr: 68.9    # mean of 69.4/68.4/66.2/68.2\n      pi05_random_k03_object_sr: 34.3    # mean of 36.4/32.2\n\n      pi05_l2norm_k095_object_sr: 98.2\n      pi05_l2norm_k0925_object_sr: 99.2\n      pi05_l2norm_k09_object_sr: 98.2    # plateau\n      pi05_l2norm_k085_object_sr: 98.0   # plateau\n      pi05_l2norm_k07_object_sr: 56.4    # mean of 55.0/57.8/56.4/56.8\n      pi05_l2norm_k05_object_sr: 33.5    # mean of 33.4/33.6/32.0\n      pi05_l2norm_k03_object_sr: 53.2    # mean of 51.0/55.4/59.0\n\n      # Spatial suite — NO catastrophic cliff, graceful degradation\n      pi05_random_k095_spatial_sr: 76.6   # mean of 76.4/76.8\n      pi05_random_k0925_spatial_sr: 59.3  # mean of 60.4/58.2\n      pi05_random_k09_spatial_sr: 54.0    # mean of 54.6/53.4/54.0\n      pi05_random_k085_spatial_sr: 58.8   # mean of 58.4/60.8/59.2/57.6\n      pi05_random_k07_spatial_sr: 74.1    # mean of 74.4/73.8\n      pi05_random_k05_spatial_sr: 72.0    # mean of 71.6/72.4/71.8\n      pi05_random_k03_spatial_sr: 48.4    # mean of 49.6/43.4/51.2\n      pi05_l2norm_k095_spatial_sr: 97.9   # mean of 97.8/98.0\n      pi05_l2norm_k09_spatial_sr: 95.3    # mean of 95.0/96.0/96.2/95.6\n      pi05_l2norm_k085_spatial_sr: 88.8   # mean of 88.6/88.4/90.4/88.2/87.4\n      pi05_l2norm_k07_spatial_sr: 67.7    # mean of 67.0/68.2/68.4\n      pi05_l2norm_k05_spatial_sr: 55.7    # mean of 55.6/55.4/57.4/58.2\n      pi05_l2norm_k03_spatial_sr: 55.0    # mean of 57.2/52.0/52.8\n\n      # Goal suite — Axis-2 amplification WEAK for π0.5 (<15pp)\n      pi05_random_k095_goal_sr: 83.5     # mean of 83.8/82.6/83.4\n      pi05_random_k09_goal_sr: 61.7      # mean of 61.8/62.2/58.0\n      pi05_random_k085_goal_sr: 52.6     # mean of 52.4/52.8/53.4/52.2\n      pi05_random_k07_goal_sr: 76.9      # mean of 78.2/75.6\n      pi05_random_k05_goal_sr: 73.6\n      pi05_random_k03_goal_sr: 51.7      # mean of 50.6/52.8\n      pi05_l2norm_k095_goal_sr: 90.1     # mean of 90.8/89.4/89.8\n      pi05_l2norm_k0925_goal_sr: 89.6    # mean of 89.0/89.8/90.8\n      pi05_l2norm_k09_goal_sr: 89.8      # mean of 88.6/90.6/91.0\n      pi05_l2norm_k085_goal_sr: 87.5     # mean of 87.4/87.0/88.0\n      pi05_l2norm_k07_goal_sr: 72.0      # mean of 70.2/73.6/72.2\n      pi05_l2norm_k05_goal_sr: 59.5      # mean of 59.8/59.2\n      pi05_l2norm_k03_goal_sr: 51.8      # mean of 50.6/54.2\n\n      # Long suite — modest amplification\n      pi05_random_k095_long_sr: 62.2     # mean of 63.2/58.4\n      pi05_random_k09_long_sr: 31.3      # mean of 31.8/32.0\n      pi05_random_k085_long_sr: 44.3     # mean of 44.4/45.2/42.0/45.6\n      pi05_random_k07_long_sr: 66.3      # mean of 65.8/64.6/68.6\n      pi05_random_k05_long_sr: 47.6      # mean of 46.8/51.2/46.8\n      pi05_random_k03_long_sr: 28.7      # mean of 29.6/28.0/28.2/28.4\n      pi05_l2norm_k095_long_sr: 87.2     # mean of 87.0/87.4\n      pi05_l2norm_k09_long_sr: 80.3      # mean of 80.0/81.0/80.0\n      pi05_l2norm_k085_long_sr: 78.8     # mean of 78.4/79.0/78.6/77.0\n      pi05_l2norm_k07_long_sr: 63.5      # mean of 62.6/60.0/65.8/65.4\n      pi05_l2norm_k05_long_sr: 51.4      # mean of 50.2/51.4/54.0/52.6\n      pi05_l2norm_k03_long_sr: 37.5      # mean of 36.6/39.0/35.2/39.2\n\n      # Axis-2 amplification (baseline - k=0.9 random) per suite\n      axis2_amplification_object_pp: 88.0   # 98.2 - 10.2 = extreme but Object-specific cliff\n      axis2_amplification_spatial_pp: 43.2   # 97.2 - 54.0\n      axis2_amplification_goal_pp: 34.7      # 96.4 - 61.7\n      axis2_amplification_long_pp: 61.5      # 92.8 - 31.3\n\n      # Key: π0.5 Goal/Long amplification comparison\n      # π0.5 Object-to-Goal diff at k=0.9 random: 10.2→61.7 = GOAL is BETTER, not worse\n      # This means Axis-2 does NOT amplify damage for token-independent connector\n      pi05_axis2_object_vs_goal_random_k09_pp: -51.5  # Goal BETTER than Object by 51.5pp\n      pi05_axis2_object_vs_spatial_random_k09_pp: -43.8  # Spatial BETTER than Object\n\n      # CV scaling law at k=0.5 (L2norm-Random gap)\n      pi05_l2norm_random_gap_k05_object_pp: -35.4  # 33.5 - 68.9 = -35.4 (random much better)\n      pi05_l2norm_random_gap_k05_spatial_pp: -16.3  # 55.7 - 72.0 = -16.3\n      pi05_l2norm_random_gap_k05_goal_pp: -14.1     # 59.5 - 73.6 = -14.1\n      pi05_l2norm_random_gap_k05_long_pp: 3.8       # 51.4 - 47.6 = +3.8 (L2norm slightly better)\n\n      # k=0.3 reversal\n      pi05_l2norm_random_gap_k03_object_pp: 18.9  # 53.2 - 34.3 = +18.9 (L2norm wins!)\n      pi05_l2norm_random_gap_k03_spatial_pp: 6.6   # 55.0 - 48.4\n      pi05_l2norm_random_gap_k03_goal_pp: 0.1      # 51.8 - 51.7 ≈ 0\n      pi05_l2norm_random_gap_k03_long_pp: 8.8      # 37.5 - 28.7\n\n    result_rationale: >\n      Median tier 下 π0.5 数据呈现三个关键 pattern：\n\n      (1) Random cliff 是 Object-specific。Object suite 在 k=0.85-0.925 出现灾难性 dip\n      (5%→10.8%→27.6%)，但 Spatial 的 floor 保持在 54% 以上，Goal 在 k=0.9 仍有 61.7%。\n      这是因为 Object 任务需要精确的 object identity discrimination（视觉相似物体间区分），\n      而 random 在 cliff zone 恰好破坏了 concentrated critical tokens。Spatial 的关键信息\n      是分布式的（layout patches），Goal 的关键信息由 language 部分承载。\n\n      (2) Axis-2 amplification 对 π0.5 表现为 REVERSED pattern：Goal 和 Spatial 在 k=0.9\n      random 下反而 BETTER than Object（61.7% vs 10.2%）。这与 X-VLA 的 pattern 完全相反\n      （X-VLA Goal k=0.9 比 Object 差 27.8pp）。原因：token-independent connector 下，\n      pruning damage 是 local 的，不会 cascade。Object 的 cliff 是 random sampling 的\n      统计效应（concentrated critical tokens），不是 task complexity amplification。\n      因此 median tier 预测 π0.5 的 Axis-2 amplification <15pp（如果排除 Object cliff zone），\n      需要在 paper 中 qualify 2-axis framework 对 token-independent connector 的适用性。\n\n      (3) CV scaling law 在 k=0.5 成立：L2norm-random gap = -35.4pp（Object），与 CV=0.055\n      的极低值一致。但 k=0.3 出现 reversal：L2norm 反而 +18.9pp 领先。这是因为 k=0.3\n      保留 230 tokens（足够大的 budget），L2norm 的 spatial clustering 在此 budget 下\n      反而 fragment 成多个 cluster，恢复了 spatial coverage。k=0.5 是 clustering 最严重的\n      sweet spot（1 cluster, 100% concentration, 78% coverage）。\n\n    tables:\n      - caption: \"π0.5 Cross-Suite Random Pruning — Cliff Zone Comparison\"\n        columns: [\"Suite\", \"k=0.95\", \"k=0.925\", \"k=0.9\", \"k=0.85\", \"k=0.7\", \"k=0.5\", \"k=0.3\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Object\", \"72.5%\", \"28.8%\", \"10.2%\", \"4.4%\", \"75.5%\", \"68.9%\", \"34.3%\"]\n          - [\"Spatial\", \"76.6%\", \"59.3%\", \"54.0%\", \"58.8%\", \"74.1%\", \"72.0%\", \"48.4%\"]\n          - [\"Goal\", \"83.5%\", \"—\", \"61.7%\", \"52.6%\", \"76.9%\", \"73.6%\", \"51.7%\"]\n          - [\"Long\", \"62.2%\", \"—\", \"31.3%\", \"44.3%\", \"66.3%\", \"47.6%\", \"28.7%\"]\n      - caption: \"π0.5 L2norm vs Random Gap (pp) — CV Scaling Law Validation\"\n        columns: [\"Suite\", \"k=0.7\", \"k=0.5\", \"k=0.3\", \"Pattern\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Object\", \"-19.1\", \"-35.4\", \"+18.9\", \"Reversal at k=0.3\"]\n          - [\"Spatial\", \"-6.4\", \"-16.3\", \"+6.6\", \"Reversal at k=0.3\"]\n          - [\"Goal\", \"-4.9\", \"-14.1\", \"+0.1\", \"Near-zero at k=0.3\"]\n          - [\"Long\", \"-2.8\", \"+3.8\", \"+8.8\", \"L2norm consistently better\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: π0.5 random pruning cliff profile — Object (deep V-shape dip to 4.4% at k=0.85) vs Spatial (gradual, floor >54%) vs Goal/Long. Key visual: Object-specific catastrophic collapse.\"\n      - \"Fig: L2norm-Random gap vs keep ratio across 4 suites — showing k=0.5 as peak random advantage and k=0.3 reversal point.\"\n    analysis: >\n      Median tier 下需要在 paper 中加 qualification：2-axis framework 的 Axis-2 (task complexity)\n      对 token-independent connector 的 amplification effect 显著弱于 token-entangling connector。\n      π0.5 的 suite-dependent sensitivity 主要由 Object cliff（random sampling + concentrated\n      critical tokens 的统计效应）驱动，而非 task complexity amplification。\n      Claim 1 需弱化为 'connector architecture is the primary determinant; task complexity is a\n      modulating factor primarily for token-entangling connectors'。\n      CV scaling law (Claim 5) 在 k=0.5 清晰成立但 k=0.3 reversal 需要限定讨论——\n      Long suite 在所有 k 值 L2norm 都不差于 random，可能是 Long 任务的 multi-step 结构\n      使得 importance-based selection 的 token 恰好 cover 关键 subgoal transitions。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # 2. Cross-Suite Expansion (plan_id: c6_libero_suite_expansion)\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"Cross-Suite Framework Validation — 5 Models × 4 Suites\"\n    plan_id: c6_libero_suite_expansion\n    description: >\n      将 pruning 实验从 LIBERO-Object 扩展到 Spatial/Goal/Long。\n      验证 2-axis framework 跨 suite 的预测准确性。\n      Median tier 预测 framework accuracy 75-90%。\n    expected_results:\n      # X-VLA cross-suite (Axis-2 amplification — strongest evidence)\n      xvla_baseline_object: 99.2\n      xvla_baseline_spatial: 93.0\n      xvla_baseline_goal: 98.4\n      xvla_baseline_long: 94.0\n\n      xvla_l2norm_k09_object: 97.6\n      xvla_l2norm_k09_spatial: 78.8\n      xvla_l2norm_k09_goal: 70.2\n      xvla_l2norm_k09_long: 27.5\n\n      xvla_random_k09_object: 97.8\n      xvla_random_k09_spatial: 77.8\n      xvla_random_k09_goal: 70.6\n      xvla_random_k09_long: 29.6\n\n      # X-VLA Axis-2 amplification at k=0.9\n      xvla_drop_k09_object_pp: 1.6   # 99.2 - 97.6\n      xvla_drop_k09_spatial_pp: 14.2  # 93.0 - 78.8\n      xvla_drop_k09_goal_pp: 28.2     # 98.4 - 70.2\n      xvla_drop_k09_long_pp: 66.5     # 94.0 - 27.5\n\n      # X-VLA k=0.5 cross-suite — random vs l2norm\n      xvla_l2norm_k05_object: 43.4\n      xvla_random_k05_object: 70.3\n      xvla_l2norm_k05_spatial: 58.9\n      xvla_random_k05_spatial: 71.4\n      xvla_l2norm_k05_goal: 59.5\n      xvla_random_k05_goal: 67.9\n      xvla_l2norm_k05_long: 44.8\n      xvla_random_k05_long: 61.6\n\n      # SmolVLA cross-suite — all cliff-edge\n      smolvla_baseline_object: 59.2\n      smolvla_baseline_spatial: 44.6\n      smolvla_baseline_goal: 60.8\n      smolvla_baseline_long: 36.6\n      smolvla_k095_all_suites_all_methods: 0  # 0% across all suites\n\n      # Framework prediction accuracy\n      framework_correct_predictions: 17\n      framework_total_predictions: 20\n      framework_accuracy_pct: 85\n\n      # Edge cases that need qualification\n      edge_case_1: \"π0.5 Axis-2 reversed — Goal BETTER than Object at k=0.9\"\n      edge_case_2: \"X-VLA Long k=0.85 non-monotonic (35%) < k=0.5 (61.6%)\"\n      edge_case_3: \"CV scaling law k=0.3 reversal for low-CV models\"\n\n    result_rationale: >\n      Median tier framework accuracy ~85%：20 个 cross-suite predictions 中 17 个正确。\n\n      正确的 predictions：\n      - X-VLA Axis-2 amplification Object→Goal/Long（confirmed 27.8pp/66.5pp）\n      - SmolVLA all suites cliff-edge（confirmed 0% everywhere）\n      - OpenVLA graded degradation across suites\n      - CV scaling law at k=0.5（L2norm-random gap correlates with CV）\n      - L2norm plateau for π0.5 at k≥0.85 on all suites\n\n      需要 qualify 的 edge cases：\n      (1) π0.5 的 Axis-2 pattern 是 reversed（Object WORST, not Goal/Long），因为\n      token-independent connector 下 task complexity 不 amplify damage，而 Object 的\n      concentrated critical tokens 在 random cliff zone 反而最脆弱。\n      (2) X-VLA Long k=0.85 出现 non-monotonic reversal（35% < k=0.5 的 61.6%），\n      与 Object 的 non-monotonic pattern 不同——Long 的 cliff zone 在更高 k 值，\n      因为 multi-step reasoning 对 token density 的 threshold 更高。\n      (3) CV scaling law k=0.3 reversal 限制了 Claim 5 的适用范围。\n\n    tables:\n      - caption: \"2-Axis Framework — X-VLA Pruning Drop at k=0.9 Across Suites\"\n        columns: [\"Suite\", \"Baseline\", \"L2norm k=0.9\", \"Drop (pp)\", \"Axis-2 Level\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Object\", \"99.2%\", \"97.6%\", \"-1.6\", \"Simple\"]\n          - [\"Spatial\", \"93.0%\", \"78.8%\", \"-14.2\", \"Moderate\"]\n          - [\"Goal\", \"98.4%\", \"70.2%\", \"-28.2\", \"Complex\"]\n          - [\"Long\", \"94.0%\", \"27.5%\", \"-66.5\", \"Most Complex\"]\n      - caption: \"Cross-Suite L2norm vs Random Gap at k=0.5 (pp) — CV Scaling Law\"\n        columns: [\"Model\", \"CV\", \"Object\", \"Spatial\", \"Goal\", \"Long\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"pi0.5\", \"0.055\", \"-35.4\", \"-16.3\", \"-14.1\", \"+3.8\"]\n          - [\"X-VLA\", \"0.151\", \"-26.9\", \"-12.5\", \"-8.4\", \"-16.8\"]\n          - [\"OpenVLA\", \"0.215\", \"+1.8\", \"—\", \"—\", \"—\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: Heatmap of pruning drop (pp from baseline) — 5 models × 4 suites × k=0.9. Visual shows clear Axis-1 (rows) and Axis-2 (columns) gradients for X-VLA/SmolVLA, but flat for π0.5/OpenVLA across suites.\"\n    analysis: >\n      Framework accuracy 85% 落在 median tier range [75%, 90%] 中。3 个 edge cases 需要在\n      paper 中 qualify：(1) 对 π0.5 等 token-independent model，用 'connector architecture\n      determines base sensitivity; task semantics modulate through statistical token criticality\n      rather than cascading damage' 替代原先的 'task complexity amplifies'。\n      (2) X-VLA Long 的 non-monotonic pattern 需要额外 figure 说明 cliff zone 随 task\n      complexity 右移。(3) k=0.3 reversal 在 Discussion 中说明 CV scaling law 的边界条件。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # 3. VTR Cross-Suite Generalization (plan_id: c6_libero_suite_vtr)\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"VTR SmolVLA Cross-Suite Recovery (M=32 on Spatial/Goal/Long)\"\n    plan_id: c6_libero_suite_vtr\n    description: >\n      VTR M=32 在 Spatial/Goal/Long 上的 recovery 验证。\n      已有数据：M=32 Spatial=53.2%, Goal=56.4%。\n      Median tier 预测 recovery ratio 0.9-1.0。\n    expected_results:\n      # SmolVLA baselines (official checkpoint)\n      smolvla_baseline_object: 59.2\n      smolvla_baseline_spatial: 44.6\n      smolvla_baseline_goal: 60.8\n      smolvla_baseline_long: 36.6\n\n      # Hard pruning reference — all 0%\n      smolvla_prune_k05_all_suites: 0\n\n      # VTR M=32 recovery\n      vtr_m32_object_sr: 60.1        # 3-seed mean (confirmed)\n      vtr_m32_spatial_sr: 53.2       # confirmed\n      vtr_m32_goal_sr: 56.4          # confirmed\n      vtr_m32_long_sr: 35.0          # predicted: Long baseline only 36.6%, VTR recovers ~95%\n\n      # Recovery ratios\n      vtr_recovery_ratio_object: 1.015  # 60.1/59.2\n      vtr_recovery_ratio_spatial: 1.193 # 53.2/44.6 — exceeds baseline (different checkpoint)\n      vtr_recovery_ratio_goal: 0.928    # 56.4/60.8\n      vtr_recovery_ratio_long: 0.956    # 35.0/36.6\n\n      # Mean recovery ratio across suites\n      vtr_mean_recovery_ratio: 0.96\n\n      # VTR M-sweep on Object (confirmed)\n      vtr_m16_object_sr: 56.9\n      vtr_m32_object_sr_confirmed: 60.1\n      vtr_m64_object_sr: 62.0\n      vtr_m96_object_sr: 54.5\n      vtr_m128_object_sr: 58.0\n\n    result_rationale: >\n      Median tier 下 VTR 在所有 suites 都能从 0%（hard pruning）恢复到 near-baseline，\n      但 recovery ratio 有 suite-dependent variation（0.928-1.193）。\n\n      Object (recovery 1.015): VTR 在 Object 上 recovery 最稳定，因为 Object 任务的 visual\n      discriminability 需求可以被 re-encoded tokens 完整保留——pixel-shuffle 的 spatial\n      entanglement 是 Object failure 的唯一原因，VTR 修复了这个 entanglement。\n\n      Spatial (recovery 1.193): 看似超过 baseline 但需注意 baseline 是 official checkpoint\n      (44.6%) vs VTR 是 LoRA-FT + VTC (53.2%)——实际上是不同 training pipeline 的差异，\n      不应解读为 VTR 超越。Paper 中需要用 recovery from 0% 而非 absolute comparison。\n\n      Goal (recovery 0.928): 轻微低于 baseline（-4.4pp），因为 VTR 是在 Object suite 训练的，\n      Goal 的 multi-step task structure 引入了 distribution shift。Token re-encoding 恢复了\n      spatial information 但无法完全补偿 task-distribution mismatch。\n\n      Long (predicted 0.956): Long 的 baseline 最低（36.6%），VTR 的 re-encoding 在 simple\n      manipulation primitives 上有效，但 Long 需要跨多个 sub-goal 的 temporal coherence，\n      VTR 的 per-step re-encoding 无法显式捕捉 cross-step dependencies。预测 recovery ~35%，\n      略低于 baseline 但远高于 0%。\n\n      关键限定：VTR 仅对 pixel-shuffle connector 有效（OpenVLA M=128 = 0%），method\n      contribution 限于 'targeted solution for worst-case architecture'。\n\n    tables:\n      - caption: \"VTR M=32 Cross-Suite Recovery from Cliff-Edge\"\n        columns: [\"Suite\", \"Baseline\", \"Hard Prune k=0.5\", \"VTR M=32\", \"Recovery Ratio\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Object\", \"59.2%\", \"0%\", \"60.1%\", \"1.015\"]\n          - [\"Spatial\", \"44.6%*\", \"0%\", \"53.2%\", \"1.193*\"]\n          - [\"Goal\", \"60.8%\", \"0%\", \"56.4%\", \"0.928\"]\n          - [\"Long\", \"36.6%\", \"0%\", \"~35.0%\", \"~0.956\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: Bar chart — SmolVLA Baseline vs Hard Prune vs VTR M=32 across 4 suites. Visual emphasis on recovery from 0% (red) to near-baseline (green).\"\n    analysis: >\n      VTR 的 mean recovery ratio 0.96 落在 median tier range [0.9, 1.0] 中。\n      Method contribution 需明确限定为 pixel-shuffle-specific：(1) 只在 SmolVLA 上有效，\n      (2) 在非 Object suite 上有 -4.4pp 到 +8.6pp 的 variance，(3) OpenVLA VTR = 0%。\n      Paper identity 从 'analysis + method' 调整为 'primarily analysis with targeted\n      method for worst-case architecture'。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # 4. VTR on OpenVLA — Method Universality Test (plan_id: c4_ext_method_universality_openvla)\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"VTR/VTC on OpenVLA (MLP projector) — Universality Falsification\"\n    plan_id: c4_ext_method_universality_openvla\n    description: >\n      VTR M=128 已确认 0% SR（overfitting）。VTC-only M=32/M=64 training in progress。\n      Median tier 预测 VTC-only 也失败，VTR 限于 pixel-shuffle。\n    expected_results:\n      # Confirmed\n      openvla_vtr_m128_20k_sr: 0     # overfitting, identical action output\n      openvla_baseline_object_sr: 74\n\n      # Predicted VTC-only results (median tier: also fail)\n      openvla_vtc_m32_sr: 0           # predicted: same overfitting pattern\n      openvla_vtc_m64_sr: 0           # predicted: same overfitting pattern\n      openvla_vtc_m96_sr: 0           # confirmed failed training\n\n      # Training diagnostics\n      openvla_vtc_m32_train_loss: 2.5  # high, indicates poor convergence\n      openvla_vtc_m64_train_loss: 2.4\n      openvla_vtc_m96_train_loss: 2.45\n\n    result_rationale: >\n      Median tier 预测 VTC-only M=32/M=64 也会失败，原因是 MLP projector tokens 已经是\n      individually meaningful 的——re-encoding 增加了不必要的 bottleneck，导致 overfitting。\n\n      具体机制：OpenVLA 的 3-layer MLP connector 将 SigLIP features 映射为 256 个独立的\n      vision tokens，每个 token 保留了原始 spatial meaning。VTR/VTC 在这些 tokens 上\n      添加 cross-attention / MLP adapter 作为 bottleneck，但这些 tokens 不需要\n      're-encoding'——它们的 spatial information 没有被 entangle。额外的 bottleneck\n      反而限制了 information flow，导致模型 overfit 到 training set 的 action distribution。\n\n      实际 training logs 显示 M=128 在 20K steps 后 output 是 identical action（所有\n      observation 产生相同的 action sequence），这是 severe mode collapse 的 hallmark。\n      M=32/M=64 的更强 compression 会加剧而非缓解这个问题。\n\n      Training 失败的 root cause 也可能是 OpenVLA 的 7B model size 导致 VTC 的 22M params\n      相对过小（0.3% of model）——gradient signal 在 backprop 过程中被 diluted。\n\n      这个 negative result 反而 strengthens 论文：VTR 的有效性是 connector-dependent 的，\n      验证了 'connector determines both compressibility AND optimal compression strategy'。\n\n    tables:\n      - caption: \"VTR/VTC on OpenVLA vs SmolVLA — Connector-Dependent Effectiveness\"\n        columns: [\"Model\", \"Connector\", \"CV\", \"VTR M=128\", \"VTC M=32\", \"VTC M=64\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"SmolVLA\", \"Pixel-shuffle\", \"0.314\", \"58.0%\", \"60.1%\", \"62.0%\"]\n          - [\"OpenVLA\", \"3-layer MLP\", \"0.215\", \"0%\", \"~0%*\", \"~0%*\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: Training loss curves — SmolVLA VTC (converges to ~0.05) vs OpenVLA VTC (plateaus at ~2.5, fails to converge). Annotate divergence point.\"\n    analysis: >\n      VTR universality falsified。Method contribution 收窄为 pixel-shuffle-specific solution。\n      Paper 中将 VTR 定位为 'targeted re-encoding for architectures where token pruning\n      creates irreversible information loss'。Discussion 中指出 MLP projector VLAs 应\n      直接用 simple pruning（L2norm 或 random depending on CV），不需要 learned compression。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # 5. OpenVLA VTC M-Sweep (plan_id: c4_ext_openvla_msweep)\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"OpenVLA VTC M-Sweep (M=32/64/96) — Training Convergence Test\"\n    plan_id: c4_ext_openvla_msweep\n    description: >\n      OpenVLA 上 VTC-only training（不冻结 backbone），测试不同 M 值。\n      Training 已 failed/killed on all M values。\n    expected_results:\n      openvla_vtc_m32_status: \"failed\"\n      openvla_vtc_m64_status: \"failed\"\n      openvla_vtc_m96_status: \"failed\"\n      openvla_vtc_m96_final_loss: 2.45\n      openvla_vtc_m64_final_loss: null  # crashed\n      interpretation: \"VTC training does not converge on MLP-projector VLAs\"\n\n    result_rationale: >\n      All M values 的 VTC training 在 OpenVLA 上失败或 killed。M=96 跑完了 100K steps\n      但 final loss 2.45（远高于 SmolVLA 的 ~0.05），说明模型未能学到有效的 token\n      re-encoding。M=64 和 M=32 的 VTC-only training 也 crashed/failed。\n\n      Root cause：OpenVLA (7B) 是 frozen backbone + 22M compressor 的极端不平衡。\n      SmolVLA (450M) 的 compressor/backbone ratio = 22M/450M = 4.9%，而 OpenVLA 的\n      ratio = 22M/7B = 0.3%。VTC 的 gradient signal 在通过 7B frozen backbone 的\n      attention layers 时被严重 attenuate，导致 compressor 无法学到有用的 representation。\n\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      OpenVLA VTC M-sweep 的 universal failure 进一步确认 VTR/VTC 仅对 pixel-shuffle\n      connector 有效。Paper 中在 Table 5 或 supplementary 中报告这些 negative results，\n      强化 'VTR effectiveness is connector-dependent' 的 claim。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # 6. OFT Graded Degradation (plan_id: c3_oft_graded_full)\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"OpenVLA-OFT Cross-Suite Pruning (Blocked by GPU Incompatibility)\"\n    plan_id: c3_oft_graded_full\n    description: >\n      OFT (7B, 3-layer MLP, DINOv2+SigLIP fused, 512 tokens) 在 4 suites 上的\n      baseline + pruning。Blocked by Blackwell GPU SDPA incompatibility。\n      Median tier 用 CV/entropy analysis 替代 SR eval。\n    expected_results:\n      # Confirmed diagnostic metrics\n      oft_cv: 0.219\n      oft_entropy: 0.667\n      oft_tokens: 512\n      oft_baseline_official_sr: 97  # cited from original paper\n\n      # Predicted pruning behavior (from CV analogy with OpenVLA CV=0.215)\n      oft_predicted_k09_sr: 65    # slightly worse than OpenVLA (62%) due to 512 tokens\n      oft_predicted_k07_sr: 50\n      oft_predicted_k05_sr: 38\n      oft_predicted_k03_sr: 22\n\n      # L2norm vs random gap (predicted from CV=0.219 ≈ OpenVLA)\n      oft_l2norm_random_gap_k05_pp: -2  # near-zero, consistent with high-CV pattern\n      oft_l2norm_advantage_mild_k: true  # L2norm slightly better at k≥0.7\n\n      # Why we can't run this\n      blocker: \"Blackwell GPU SDPA incompatibility — requires A100 + torch 2.2\"\n\n    result_rationale: >\n      OFT eval 被 Blackwell GPU 的 SDPA 不兼容 blocked。Median tier 下仅用 diagnostic\n      metrics 参与分析：CV=0.219 ≈ OpenVLA (0.215)，entropy=0.667 ≈ OpenVLA (0.661)。\n      \n      这两个 near-identical diagnostic values 预测 OFT 的 pruning behavior 与 OpenVLA\n      几乎一致——graded degradation，L2norm 在 aggressive k 略优于 random。\n      512 tokens (vs OpenVLA 的 256) 意味着 absolute token budget 在 same k ratio 下\n      更大（k=0.5 保留 256 vs 128），可能导致略好的 SR，但 degradation PATTERN 应相同。\n\n      关键 paper value：OFT 用了不同的 action head（Optimal Flow Transport vs standard），\n      但 CV 和 entropy 几乎 identical → 确认 connector（not action head）determines\n      attention structure 和 pruning behavior。这是一个 clean controlled comparison。\n\n      Median tier 下 OFT 作为 supplementary evidence 出现（CV/entropy table），\n      不作为 primary experimental evidence。Cite official baseline ~97%，\n      acknowledge eval 未能完成。\n\n    tables:\n      - caption: \"Connector vs Action Head — Diagnostic Decoupling\"\n        columns: [\"Model\", \"Action Head\", \"Connector\", \"CV\", \"Entropy\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"OpenVLA\", \"Standard (MLP)\", \"3-layer MLP\", \"0.215\", \"0.661\"]\n          - [\"OpenVLA-OFT\", \"OFT (flow)\", \"3-layer MLP\", \"0.219\", \"0.667\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: Scatter plot of CV vs Entropy for all 6 models — OFT and OpenVLA as overlapping points, confirming connector-dominance over action-head.\"\n    analysis: >\n      OFT 贡献收窄为 diagnostic decoupling evidence。Paper 中用一句话总结：\n      'OFT (CV=0.219) ≈ Standard OpenVLA (CV=0.215) despite different action heads,\n      confirming that connector architecture, not downstream components, determines\n      token importance distribution.' Eval SR 不可得，acknowledged as limitation。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # 7. OFT CV Diagnostic (plan_id: diagnostic_oft_cv)\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"OFT Token Importance CV Measurement\"\n    plan_id: diagnostic_oft_cv\n    description: >\n      OFT importance CV 测量，完成 6-model diagnostic table 的最后一个空位。\n    expected_results:\n      oft_importance_cv: 0.219\n      oft_importance_cv_std: 0.012\n      oft_importance_gini: 0.11\n      oft_n_tokens: 512\n      spectrum_position: \"between OpenVLA (0.215) and SmolVLA (0.314)\"\n\n    result_rationale: >\n      OFT 使用与 OpenVLA 相同的 3-layer MLP connector（GELU activation），唯一差异是\n      (1) fused DINOv2+SigLIP encoder 产生 512 tokens（vs OpenVLA 的 256），\n      (2) OFT action head。Entropy 已确认 0.667 ≈ 0.661，CV 预测 0.219 ≈ 0.215。\n      微小的 CV 差异（+0.004）可能来自 DINOv2 features 的 additional modality 引入的\n      slightly higher token heterogeneity。\n\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      CV=0.219 完成 6-model spectrum：π0(0.038) < π0.5(0.055) < X-VLA(0.151) <\n      OpenVLA(0.215) ≈ OFT(0.219) < SmolVLA(0.314)。\n      Paper Table 1 中 OFT 行填入 CV=0.219, Entropy=0.667, Pruning='Graded (predicted)'。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # 8. X-VLA Cliff Localization (plan_id: c1_xvla_threshold_localization)\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"X-VLA k=0.8/k=0.85 3-Seed Cliff Localization\"\n    plan_id: c1_xvla_threshold_localization\n    description: >\n      X-VLA Object cliff threshold 精确定位：k=0.85 (67.9% ± 0.31pp, 3-seed) 和\n      k=0.80 (89.0% ± 0.72pp, 3-seed)。Non-monotonic: k=0.85 < k=0.80。\n    expected_results:\n      # L2norm 3-seed\n      xvla_l2norm_k085_object_mean: 67.9\n      xvla_l2norm_k085_object_std: 0.31\n      xvla_l2norm_k085_seeds: [68.0, 67.6, 68.2]\n      xvla_l2norm_k080_object_mean: 89.0\n      xvla_l2norm_k080_object_std: 0.72\n      xvla_l2norm_k080_seeds: [88.8, 88.4, 89.8]\n\n      # Random comparison\n      xvla_random_k085_object_mean: 64.3\n      xvla_random_k085_seeds: [65.0, 63.6, 63.2]\n      xvla_random_k080_object_mean: 89.4\n      xvla_random_k080_seeds: [89.4]\n\n      # Non-monotonicity\n      non_monotonic_gap_pp: 21.1  # k=0.80 - k=0.85 = 89.0 - 67.9\n      cliff_width_k_units: 0.05   # from k=0.85 (cliff) to k=0.80 (recovery)\n\n      # Cross-method consistency\n      l2norm_random_k085_gap_pp: 3.6  # L2norm slightly better (67.9 vs 64.3)\n      both_crash_same_tasks: true     # T1, T4, T6, T8 crash for both methods\n\n    result_rationale: >\n      3-seed deterministic data 确认 cliff 位于 k=0.85（42 tokens kept），且\n      k=0.80（40 tokens）recovery 到 89%——仅差 2 个 tokens 但 21pp gap。\n\n      Non-monotonicity 来自 BART encoder 的 length-dependent interactions：\n      - k=0.85 (42 tokens): BART 的 12-layer self-attention 在 42 tokens 上产生\n        destructive interference pattern——刚好是 critical token density threshold\n      - k=0.80 (40 tokens): 少保留 2 个 tokens 反而破坏了这个 interference pattern，\n        恢复了正常的 information flow\n\n      SD < 1pp across all 3 seeds 确认 cliff 是完全 deterministic 的（L2norm pruning\n      是 deterministic function of token norms），不是 stochastic noise。\n\n      L2norm 和 random 在 cliff zone 都 crash on same 4 tasks (T1=cream_cheese,\n      T4=ketchup, T6=butter, T8=chocolate_pudding) → cliff 是 architectural，\n      不是 method-specific。\n\n    tables:\n      - caption: \"X-VLA Object Cliff Zone — 3-Seed Deterministic (L2norm)\"\n        columns: [\"k\", \"Tokens Kept\", \"Seed 42\", \"Seed 43\", \"Seed 44\", \"Mean\", \"SD\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"0.90\", \"45\", \"97.6%\", \"—\", \"98.2%\", \"97.6%\", \"—\"]\n          - [\"0.85\", \"42\", \"68.0%\", \"67.6%\", \"68.2%\", \"67.9%\", \"0.31\"]\n          - [\"0.80\", \"40\", \"88.8%\", \"88.4%\", \"89.8%\", \"89.0%\", \"0.72\"]\n          - [\"0.70\", \"35\", \"56.2%\", \"59.0%\", \"56.4%\", \"57.2%\", \"1.56\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: X-VLA Object cliff profile with 3-seed error bars — sharp V-shape at k=0.85, recovery at k=0.80. Annotate '2 tokens, 21pp gap'.\"\n    analysis: >\n      Cliff localization 完成。Paper 中用 1 figure 展示 X-VLA 的 full pruning curve\n      (k=0.1 to k=0.95)，annotate k=0.85 cliff 和 non-monotonic recovery。\n      Discussion 中说明 BART encoder 的 length-dependent interaction 机制。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # 9. Perceiver Resampler — 3rd Connector Family (plan_id: c5_third_connector_roboflamingo)\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"RoboFlamingo Perceiver Resampler Fine-tune + Pruning\"\n    plan_id: c5_third_connector_roboflamingo\n    description: >\n      Perceiver Resampler connector 作为第 3 个 connector family 验证。\n      Training killed twice。Median tier 预测即使完成也不会改变核心结论。\n    expected_results:\n      # Training status\n      training_status: \"killed\"\n      training_attempts: 2\n\n      # Predicted results IF training succeeded\n      roboflamingo_predicted_cv: 0.18     # between X-VLA (0.151) and OpenVLA (0.215)\n      roboflamingo_predicted_entropy: 0.72\n      roboflamingo_predicted_baseline_sr: 55  # lower baseline due to smaller model\n      roboflamingo_predicted_k09_sr: 48       # moderate degradation\n      roboflamingo_predicted_k05_sr: 28       # significant degradation\n\n      # Paper impact\n      would_strengthen_paper: false   # marginal value — already have 5 models\n      paper_coverage_without: \"5 models × 3 families sufficient for CoRL\"\n\n    result_rationale: >\n      RoboFlamingo training 两次 killed，likely due to (1) Perceiver Resampler 与 LIBERO\n      task distribution 的 incompatibility，(2) fine-tuning instability from frozen\n      cross-attention + trainable resampler 的 gradient mismatch。\n\n      即使完成，Perceiver Resampler 的预测 CV=0.18 会落在 X-VLA 和 OpenVLA 之间——\n      介于 token-entangling 和 token-independent 之间。这不会改变 2-axis framework\n      的核心结论，只是增加一个中间数据点。\n\n      Median tier 下 5 models × 3 families (linear / MLP / pixel-shuffle) 已经足够\n      支撑 CoRL submission。Perceiver Resampler 作为 'future work' 提及。\n\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      Dropped from paper scope。在 Discussion 中提到 'additional connector families\n      (e.g., Perceiver Resampler, cross-attention based) remain to be validated'\n      作为 limitation 和 future direction。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # 10. E5 Attention Pruning — Additional Method (cross-cutting)\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"E5 Attention-Based Pruning — X-VLA vs π0.5 Cross-Suite\"\n    plan_id: c6_libero_suite_expansion\n    description: >\n      Attention-based pruning (E5) 在 X-VLA 和 π0.5 上的 cross-suite 结果。\n      X-VLA attention pruning 表现极好（Object 99.2%, Long 90.2%），\n      π0.5 attention 在 Object k=0.7 catastrophic (0.6%) 但 Goal 70.2%。\n      Median tier：Goal 初始 0% 后修复为 98.2%，需额外 seed 确认可靠性。\n    expected_results:\n      # X-VLA E5 attention pruning (confirmed — near-lossless)\n      xvla_attn_last_k05_object: 99.2\n      xvla_attn_mean_k05_object: 98.4\n      xvla_attn_rollout_k05_object: 97.4\n      xvla_attn_last_k05_spatial: 88.8\n      xvla_attn_mean_k05_spatial: 91.6\n      xvla_attn_rollout_k05_spatial: 92.8\n      xvla_attn_last_k05_goal: 98.2   # AFTER fix (was 0% before fix)\n      xvla_attn_mean_k05_goal: 97.4\n      xvla_attn_rollout_k05_goal: 96.8\n      xvla_attn_last_k05_long: 90.2\n      xvla_attn_mean_k05_long: 94.0\n      xvla_attn_rollout_k05_long: 94.8\n\n      # X-VLA attention k=0.3 (more aggressive)\n      xvla_attn_last_k03_object: 84.2\n      xvla_attn_mean_k03_object: 96.0\n      xvla_attn_mean_k03_spatial: 90.4\n      xvla_attn_last_k03_spatial: 85.6\n\n      # π0.5 E5 attention pruning (mixed results)\n      pi05_attn_k095_object: 98.4    # near-lossless at mild compression\n      pi05_attn_k09_object: 97.2     # still good\n      pi05_attn_k085_object: 92.2    # starts degrading\n      pi05_attn_k07_object: 0.6      # CATASTROPHIC — attention becomes adversarial\n      pi05_attn_k05_object: 37.8     # partial recovery\n      pi05_attn_k05_spatial: 72.6    # spatial robust\n      pi05_attn_k05_goal: 71.2       # mean of 70.2/72.2\n      pi05_attn_k05_long: 49.4\n\n      # OpenVLA attention pruning\n      openvla_attn_k09_object: 61.4\n      openvla_attn_k085_object: 55.0\n      openvla_attn_k09_goal: 73.2\n      openvla_attn_k09_spatial: 80.4\n\n      # Goal fix reliability\n      xvla_attn_goal_fix_needed: true\n      xvla_attn_goal_seed42_sr: 98.2\n      xvla_attn_goal_seed43_needed: true  # additional seed for confirmation\n      xvla_attn_goal_predicted_seed43_sr: 97.5  # predicted: fix is genuine\n\n    result_rationale: >\n      E5 attention pruning 在不同 model 上表现 divergent：\n\n      X-VLA (BART encoder)：attention pruning 近乎 lossless，因为 BART 的 12-layer\n      self-attention 产生了 meaningful attention patterns——high-attention tokens 确实\n      是最重要的。k=0.5 Object 99.2% vs L2norm 42.6% → attention 比 L2norm 好 56.6pp。\n      这是因为 BART encoder 的 attention 直接反映了 token 间的 functional dependency。\n\n      Goal suite 初始为 0%（bug），修复后 98.2% → 需要 seed43 确认 fix 是 genuine。\n      Median tier 预测 seed43 = 97.5%（fix 是 valid 的，但需要额外 seed 才能在\n      paper 中 claim）。\n\n      π0.5 (linear projection)：attention pruning 在 k=0.7 catastrophic (0.6%)，\n      因为 PaliGemma 的 per-layer attention 在中间 k 值产生了 adversarial selection。\n      π0.5 的 attention entropy = 0.666，说明 attention 分布有 moderate sharpness，\n      但不 correlate with true token importance（CV=0.055 说明所有 tokens equally\n      important）。Attention-based pruning 在 uniform-importance model 上不可靠。\n\n      OpenVLA (MLP)：attention pruning k=0.9 Object = 61.4% < L2norm = 70.6% < random = 69.2%。\n      Attention 是三种方法中最差的，因为 MLP connector 后的 attention 也不 reliable\n      predict token importance。\n\n      Paper value：attention pruning 的 effectiveness 也是 connector-dependent，\n      strengthening 'connector determines optimal compression strategy' claim。\n\n    tables:\n      - caption: \"E5 Attention Pruning k=0.5 — Cross-Model Cross-Suite\"\n        columns: [\"Model\", \"Object\", \"Spatial\", \"Goal\", \"Long\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"X-VLA (attn-last)\", \"99.2%\", \"88.8%\", \"98.2%*\", \"90.2%\"]\n          - [\"X-VLA (attn-mean)\", \"98.4%\", \"91.6%\", \"97.4%\", \"94.0%\"]\n          - [\"pi0.5 (attn)\", \"37.8%\", \"72.6%\", \"71.2%\", \"49.4%\"]\n          - [\"X-VLA (L2norm)\", \"42.6%\", \"58.8%\", \"59.0%\", \"44.6%\"]\n          - [\"X-VLA (random)\", \"70.6%\", \"71.4%\", \"67.9%\", \"61.6%\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: Method comparison radar chart — X-VLA at k=0.5: attention (near-lossless) vs L2norm (42.6%) vs random (70.6%) across 4 suites. Shows attention dominance for BART connector.\"\n    analysis: >\n      E5 attention pruning 提供了 Claim 5 的重要扩展：不只是 L2norm vs random 的\n      strategy depends on CV，attention-based methods 也是 connector-dependent。\n      BART connector 的 attention 是 reliable signal（因为 12-layer self-attention\n      creates meaningful importance distribution），而 linear/MLP connector 的 attention\n      不可靠。Paper 中可以加一行 Table showing method effectiveness rank per model。\n      但 Goal 0%→98.2% 的 fix 需要 seed43 确认，Median tier 下这个 reliability concern\n      需要在 paper 中 transparent disclosure。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # 11. CV Scaling Law Consolidation (cross-cutting analysis)\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"CV Scaling Law — Spearman Correlation Across Conditions\"\n    plan_id: c6_libero_suite_expansion\n    description: >\n      CV 作为 pruning strategy predictor 的 Spearman correlation 分析。\n      Median tier 预测 abs(Spearman) 在 0.6-0.85 之间。\n    expected_results:\n      # k=0.5 scaling law (strongest)\n      cv_vs_l2norm_random_gap_k05_spearman: 0.82\n      cv_vs_l2norm_random_gap_k05_p_value: 0.03\n\n      # k=0.7 scaling law (confirmatory)\n      cv_vs_l2norm_random_gap_k07_spearman: 0.75\n      cv_vs_l2norm_random_gap_k07_p_value: 0.05\n\n      # k=0.3 scaling law (REVERSED for low-CV)\n      cv_vs_l2norm_random_gap_k03_spearman: 0.45   # weak — reversal breaks monotonicity\n      cv_vs_l2norm_random_gap_k03_p_value: 0.15    # not significant\n\n      # Cross-suite Spearman (averaging across suites)\n      cv_strategy_abs_spearman_mean: 0.74   # within [0.6, 0.85] range\n\n      # Data points used\n      n_models_k05: 3   # π0.5 (0.055), X-VLA (0.151), OpenVLA (0.215)\n      n_suites_k05: 1   # Object only for 3-model comparison\n      datapoints_k05:\n        - {model: \"pi0.5\", cv: 0.055, gap_pp: -35.4}\n        - {model: \"X-VLA\", cv: 0.151, gap_pp: -26.9}\n        - {model: \"OpenVLA\", cv: 0.215, gap_pp: 1.8}\n\n      # k=0.5 validated at two k values\n      k05_gap_monotonic: true    # -35.4 → -26.9 → +1.8\n      k07_gap_monotonic: true    # -22.2 → -6.5 → +5.4\n      k03_gap_monotonic: false   # +18.9 → -42.3 → -3.6 — NOT monotonic\n\n    result_rationale: >\n      CV scaling law 的 Spearman correlation 0.74 落在 median tier range [0.6, 0.85] 中。\n\n      k=0.5 是最 clean 的 scaling law validation point：3 个 model 的 L2norm-random gap\n      与 CV 呈单调关系（-35.4pp → -26.9pp → +1.8pp as CV increases 0.055 → 0.151 → 0.215）。\n      Spearman = 0.82，因为只有 3 个 data points 所以 p-value 边缘显著。\n\n      k=0.7 作为 confirmatory second row：pattern 一致但 gap magnitudes 小（-22.2 → -6.5 → +5.4），\n      Spearman = 0.75。\n\n      k=0.3 BREAKS the scaling law：π0.5 reversal (+18.9pp L2norm wins) 但 X-VLA\n      random 仍大幅领先 (+42.3pp)。这不是 CV 不好，而是 absolute token budget 的交互效应：\n      π0.5 k=0.3 保留 230 tokens（大 budget），X-VLA k=0.3 保留 15 tokens（小 budget）。\n      Large budget + low CV = L2norm 可以 fragment clusters 恢复 diversity。\n      Small budget + mid CV = 无论如何都太少，random 保持 stochastic diversity 的优势。\n\n      Paper strategy：k=0.5 作为 main table，k=0.7 作为 confirmatory。k=0.3 reversal\n      在 Discussion 中说明，强调 'CV predicts strategy preference at moderate compression\n      (k=0.5-0.7); at extreme compression (k=0.3), absolute token budget introduces\n      additional interaction'。Claim 5 加限定 'at moderate compression'。\n\n    tables:\n      - caption: \"CV Scaling Law — L2norm vs Random Gap (pp) at k=0.5 and k=0.7\"\n        columns: [\"Model\", \"CV\", \"Gap k=0.7 (pp)\", \"Gap k=0.5 (pp)\", \"Gap k=0.3 (pp)\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"pi0.5\", \"0.055\", \"-22.2\", \"-35.4\", \"+18.9\"]\n          - [\"X-VLA\", \"0.151\", \"-6.5\", \"-26.9\", \"-42.3\"]\n          - [\"OpenVLA\", \"0.215\", \"+5.4\", \"+1.8\", \"+3.6\"]\n      - caption: \"Spearman Correlation: CV vs Strategy Gap\"\n        columns: [\"k value\", \"Spearman rho\", \"p-value\", \"Monotonic?\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"0.7\", \"0.75\", \"0.05\", \"Yes\"]\n          - [\"0.5\", \"0.82\", \"0.03\", \"Yes\"]\n          - [\"0.3\", \"0.45\", \"0.15\", \"No (reversal)\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: Scatter plot with regression line — CV (x-axis) vs L2norm-Random gap (y-axis) at k=0.5. Three points with clear positive trend. Annotate Spearman=0.82.\"\n    analysis: >\n      Claim 5 survives review but需要加限定。原 claim 'CV predicts optimal pruning strategy'\n      改为 'CV predicts optimal pruning strategy at moderate compression (k=0.5-0.7)'。\n      k=0.3 reversal 说明 strategy preference = f(CV, k, absolute_token_budget)，\n      不是仅 CV 决定。这个 nuance 在 median tier 下是可以接受的——reviewers 会 appreciate\n      honest boundary conditions。3-4 个 claims survive review 的预测中，这个 claim\n      以 qualified form survive。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # 12. SmolVLA VTR Learned Re-encoding Consolidation (plan_id: c4_learned_reencoding_smolvla)\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"SmolVLA VTR M-Sweep 3-Seed Consolidation + Architecture Control\"\n    plan_id: c4_learned_reencoding_smolvla\n    description: >\n      VTR M-sweep (M=16/32/64/96/128) 的 3-seed 最终结果 + MLP adapter 对照。\n      已有大量数据，Median tier 下 consolidate 最终 statistics。\n    expected_results:\n      # 3-seed M-sweep (cross-attention VTC)\n      vtr_m16_3seed_mean: 56.9\n      vtr_m16_3seed_std: 1.3\n      vtr_m16_3seed_seeds: [55.8, 58.4, 56.5]\n\n      vtr_m32_3seed_mean: 60.1\n      vtr_m32_3seed_std: 1.3\n      vtr_m32_3seed_seeds: [61.6, 59.2, 59.6]\n\n      vtr_m64_3seed_mean: 62.0\n      vtr_m64_3seed_std: 2.3\n      vtr_m64_3seed_seeds: [61.6, 60.0, 64.4]\n\n      vtr_m96_3seed_mean: 54.5\n      vtr_m96_3seed_std: 3.2\n      vtr_m96_3seed_seeds: [52.6, 58.2, 52.8]\n\n      vtr_m128_3seed_mean: 58.0\n      vtr_m128_3seed_std: 3.5\n      vtr_m128_3seed_seeds: [59.8, 54.0, 60.2]\n\n      # M-curve flatness\n      m_curve_range_pp: 7.5           # max(62.0) - min(54.5)\n      m_curve_vs_baseline_max_diff: 5.3  # max deviation from baseline 59.2%\n      m_curve_flat: true\n\n      # MLP adapter control (3-seed)\n      mlp_adapter_m32_3seed_mean: 63.4\n      mlp_adapter_m32_3seed_std: 2.6\n      mlp_adapter_m32_3seed_seeds: [65.2, 64.6, 60.4]\n\n      # Architecture independence t-test\n      vtc_vs_mlp_t_stat: 1.94\n      vtc_vs_mlp_p_value: 0.15\n      architecture_independent: true\n\n      # Baseline comparison\n      smolvla_baseline: 59.2\n      hard_prune_k05: 0\n      recovery_from_zero: true\n\n    result_rationale: >\n      VTR M-sweep 确认 M-curve 是 flat 的：M=16 (56.9%) 到 M=128 (58.0%)，\n      all within ±5pp of baseline 59.2%。这意味着 VTR 对 pixel-shuffle connector\n      实现了 near-lossless compression at ANY ratio (0-87.5%)。\n\n      M=64 是 absolute best (62.0%)，M=96 是 lowest (54.5%) 但 p=0.034 与 M=64\n      的差异 statistically significant——M=96 的 higher variance (3.2pp) 和 lower mean\n      可能是因为 96-token representation 落在 an awkward regime：不够多以 passthrough\n      (M=128)，但 compression ratio 不够大 to force useful abstraction (M=32/64)。\n\n      MLP adapter (63.4%) vs VTC (60.1%) p=0.15 → architecture independent。\n      任何 learned re-encoding 都能从 0% 恢复到 baseline。\n\n      Median tier 下 VTR 的 contribution statement 明确：'VTR achieves near-lossless\n      compression at any ratio for pixel-shuffle connectors, recovering from 0%\n      (hard pruning) to ~59% (baseline)'。不 overclaim 超过 baseline。\n\n    tables:\n      - caption: \"VTR M-Sweep — 3-Seed Statistics (SmolVLA Object)\"\n        columns: [\"M\", \"Compression\", \"Mean SR (%)\", \"Std (pp)\", \"vs Baseline\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"16\", \"87.5%\", \"56.9\", \"1.3\", \"-2.3pp\"]\n          - [\"32\", \"75.0%\", \"60.1\", \"1.3\", \"+0.9pp\"]\n          - [\"64\", \"50.0%\", \"62.0\", \"2.3\", \"+2.8pp\"]\n          - [\"96\", \"25.0%\", \"54.5\", \"3.2\", \"-4.7pp\"]\n          - [\"128\", \"0% (pass)\", \"58.0\", \"3.5\", \"-1.2pp\"]\n          - [\"MLP-32\", \"75.0%\", \"63.4\", \"2.6\", \"+4.2pp\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: M-curve with error bars — flat profile, all within baseline ±5pp band (shaded). Hard prune reference at 0%.\"\n    analysis: >\n      VTR results 完备。Paper 中用 M-curve figure + architecture control table\n      支撑 Claim 4。Key limitation：仅对 pixel-shuffle 有效（OpenVLA 0%），\n      method contribution 限于 worst-case architecture。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # 13. Claims Survival Analysis — Median Tier\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"Claims Survival Under Review — Median Tier Assessment\"\n    plan_id: c6_libero_suite_expansion\n    description: >\n      5 个 core claims 在 median tier 下的 review survival 预测。\n      预测 3-4 个 claims survive。\n    expected_results:\n      claims_surviving: 3.5  # 3 full + 1 qualified\n\n      claim_1_2axis_framework:\n        status: \"survives with qualification\"\n        original: \"governed by two axes\"\n        revised: \"primarily explained by connector architecture, with task complexity as a modulating factor for token-entangling connectors\"\n        qualification: \"Axis-2 amplification weak for token-independent connectors (π0.5)\"\n        strength: 0.8\n\n      claim_2_pixel_shuffle_entanglement:\n        status: \"survives fully\"\n        evidence: \"7 conditions × 4 suites × official checkpoint → 0%\"\n        strength: 1.0\n\n      claim_3_graded_degradation:\n        status: \"survives fully\"\n        evidence: \"OpenVLA 6-point curve + OFT CV/entropy confirmation\"\n        strength: 0.95\n\n      claim_4_vtr_recovery:\n        status: \"survives with limitation\"\n        original: \"universal compression via VTR\"\n        revised: \"VTR recovers pixel-shuffle from 0% to baseline; ineffective for MLP projector\"\n        limitation: \"method contribution narrowed to pixel-shuffle-specific\"\n        strength: 0.7\n\n      claim_5_cv_scaling_law:\n        status: \"survives with boundary condition\"\n        original: \"CV predicts optimal strategy\"\n        revised: \"CV predicts optimal strategy at moderate compression (k=0.5-0.7)\"\n        boundary: \"k=0.3 reversal for low-CV models with large token budgets\"\n        strength: 0.75\n\n    result_rationale: >\n      Median tier 预测 3.5 claims survive（3 full + 1.5 qualified），落在 [3, 4] range。\n\n      Claim 2（pixel-shuffle entanglement）是最 robust 的——0% at k=0.95, all methods,\n      all suites, official checkpoint, dual-seed confirmed。没有任何 edge case。\n\n      Claim 3（graded degradation）也 robust——OpenVLA 6-point curve 是 clean monotonic，\n      OFT CV/entropy confirmation 是 clean controlled comparison。\n\n      Claim 1（2-axis framework）需要 qualification 因为 Axis-2 对 token-independent\n      connectors 的 amplification 弱于预期。Paper 不能说 'task complexity always amplifies\n      pruning sensitivity'，而是 'task complexity amplifies sensitivity SPECIFICALLY for\n      token-entangling connectors where pruning damage cascades'。\n\n      Claim 4（VTR）的 method contribution 收窄——OpenVLA 0% 意味着 VTR 不是 universal。\n      Reviewers 可能 question: 'if VTR only works on pixel-shuffle, and pixel-shuffle is\n      the architecture you're warning against, isn't the method contribution circular?'\n      Response: 'VTR provides a migration path for existing pixel-shuffle VLAs, not a\n      design recommendation for new ones.'\n\n      Claim 5（CV scaling law）加 boundary condition 后仍有价值——k=0.5-0.7 的 scaling law\n      是 clean 的（Spearman 0.75-0.82），只是 k=0.3 有 reversal。\n\n    tables:\n      - caption: \"Claims Survival Assessment — Median Tier\"\n        columns: [\"Claim\", \"Original Strength\", \"Median Tier Status\", \"Revised Strength\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"C1: 2-Axis Framework\", \"Strong\", \"Qualified\", \"0.80\"]\n          - [\"C2: Pixel-Shuffle\", \"Strong\", \"Fully Survives\", \"1.00\"]\n          - [\"C3: Graded Degradation\", \"Strong\", \"Fully Survives\", \"0.95\"]\n          - [\"C4: VTR Recovery\", \"Moderate\", \"Limited to pixel-shuffle\", \"0.70\"]\n          - [\"C5: CV Scaling Law\", \"Moderate\", \"Boundary at k=0.3\", \"0.75\"]\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      Paper identity 调整为 'primarily analysis with targeted method'。\n      Title 改为 'How Vision Connectors Shape Token Pruning Robustness in VLAs'——\n      更保守但准确。Contribution statement 聚焦：(1) first systematic cross-architecture\n      token pruning analysis in VLAs (5 models × 4 suites), (2) CV as zero-cost\n      diagnostic for pruning tolerance AND strategy, (3) VTR as targeted recovery\n      method for worst-case (pixel-shuffle) connectors。仍提交 CoRL。\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":179,"cache_read_input_tokens":130289,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":179},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f3a93c25-07a2-42fa-8e9c-436d384627d6","uuid":"71b54667-fa04-4b8a-8ab1-f5d957ba7379"}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":503406,"duration_api_ms":505841,"num_turns":5,"result":"Now I have the full experiment plan and the extensive registry data. Let me generate the median tier predictions.\n\n```yaml\ntier: median\nnarrative_guidance: >\n  2-axis framework directionally correct but需要 qualify 2-3 个 edge cases。\n  Claim 1 弱化为 'primarily explained by connector architecture, with task complexity as a modulating factor'。\n  Claim 5 加限定 'at moderate compression (k=0.5-0.7)'，k=0.3 reversal 移入 Discussion。\n  VTR 明确为 pixel-shuffle-specific solution。Paper identity 从 'analysis + method' 调整为 'primarily analysis with targeted method for worst-case architecture'。\n  Title 改为更保守的 'How Vision Connectors Shape Token Pruning Robustness in VLAs'。\n  仍提交 CoRL，contribution statement 聚焦 diagnostic insight。\n\nimagined_experiments:\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # 1. π0.5 Cross-Suite Immune Confirmation (plan_id: c1_pi05_immune_confirmation)\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"π0.5 4-Suite Pruning Characterization — Median Tier Consolidation\"\n    plan_id: c1_pi05_immune_confirmation\n    description: >\n      π0.5 (4B, PaliGemma linear proj, CV=0.055) 在 4 个 LIBERO suites 的 pruning response。\n      Median tier 预测：Object 上 random cliff (k=0.85-0.925) 是 Object-specific 而非 universal；\n      Goal/Long 上 Axis-2 amplification 弱于 X-VLA (<15pp for π0.5 vs 27.8pp for X-VLA)。\n      CV scaling law 在 k=0.5 成立但 k=0.3 reversal 需要限定讨论。\n    expected_results:\n      # Baselines (confirmed)\n      pi05_baseline_object: 98.2\n      pi05_baseline_spatial: 97.2\n      pi05_baseline_goal: 96.4\n      pi05_baseline_long: 92.8\n      pi05_cv: 0.055\n\n      # Object suite — random cliff confirmed Object-specific\n      pi05_random_k095_object_sr: 72.5  # mean of 74.0/71.1/72.8\n      pi05_random_k0925_object_sr: 28.8  # mean of 27.6/30.0\n      pi05_random_k09_object_sr: 10.2   # mean of 9.0/10.8/9.6\n      pi05_random_k085_object_sr: 4.4    # mean of 5.0/3.8/4.4\n      pi05_random_k07_object_sr: 75.5    # mean of 77.2/73.8/74.0\n      pi05_random_k05_object_sr: 68.9    # mean of 69.4/68.4/66.2/68.2\n      pi05_random_k03_object_sr: 34.3    # mean of 36.4/32.2\n\n      pi05_l2norm_k095_object_sr: 98.2\n      pi05_l2norm_k0925_object_sr: 99.2\n      pi05_l2norm_k09_object_sr: 98.2    # plateau\n      pi05_l2norm_k085_object_sr: 98.0   # plateau\n      pi05_l2norm_k07_object_sr: 56.4    # mean of 55.0/57.8/56.4/56.8\n      pi05_l2norm_k05_object_sr: 33.5    # mean of 33.4/33.6/32.0\n      pi05_l2norm_k03_object_sr: 53.2    # mean of 51.0/55.4/59.0\n\n      # Spatial suite — NO catastrophic cliff, graceful degradation\n      pi05_random_k095_spatial_sr: 76.6   # mean of 76.4/76.8\n      pi05_random_k0925_spatial_sr: 59.3  # mean of 60.4/58.2\n      pi05_random_k09_spatial_sr: 54.0    # mean of 54.6/53.4/54.0\n      pi05_random_k085_spatial_sr: 58.8   # mean of 58.4/60.8/59.2/57.6\n      pi05_random_k07_spatial_sr: 74.1    # mean of 74.4/73.8\n      pi05_random_k05_spatial_sr: 72.0    # mean of 71.6/72.4/71.8\n      pi05_random_k03_spatial_sr: 48.4    # mean of 49.6/43.4/51.2\n      pi05_l2norm_k095_spatial_sr: 97.9   # mean of 97.8/98.0\n      pi05_l2norm_k09_spatial_sr: 95.3    # mean of 95.0/96.0/96.2/95.6\n      pi05_l2norm_k085_spatial_sr: 88.8   # mean of 88.6/88.4/90.4/88.2/87.4\n      pi05_l2norm_k07_spatial_sr: 67.7    # mean of 67.0/68.2/68.4\n      pi05_l2norm_k05_spatial_sr: 55.7    # mean of 55.6/55.4/57.4/58.2\n      pi05_l2norm_k03_spatial_sr: 55.0    # mean of 57.2/52.0/52.8\n\n      # Goal suite — Axis-2 amplification WEAK for π0.5 (<15pp)\n      pi05_random_k095_goal_sr: 83.5     # mean of 83.8/82.6/83.4\n      pi05_random_k09_goal_sr: 61.7      # mean of 61.8/62.2/58.0\n      pi05_random_k085_goal_sr: 52.6     # mean of 52.4/52.8/53.4/52.2\n      pi05_random_k07_goal_sr: 76.9      # mean of 78.2/75.6\n      pi05_random_k05_goal_sr: 73.6\n      pi05_random_k03_goal_sr: 51.7      # mean of 50.6/52.8\n      pi05_l2norm_k095_goal_sr: 90.1     # mean of 90.8/89.4/89.8\n      pi05_l2norm_k0925_goal_sr: 89.6    # mean of 89.0/89.8/90.8\n      pi05_l2norm_k09_goal_sr: 89.8      # mean of 88.6/90.6/91.0\n      pi05_l2norm_k085_goal_sr: 87.5     # mean of 87.4/87.0/88.0\n      pi05_l2norm_k07_goal_sr: 72.0      # mean of 70.2/73.6/72.2\n      pi05_l2norm_k05_goal_sr: 59.5      # mean of 59.8/59.2\n      pi05_l2norm_k03_goal_sr: 51.8      # mean of 50.6/54.2\n\n      # Long suite — modest amplification\n      pi05_random_k095_long_sr: 62.2     # mean of 63.2/58.4\n      pi05_random_k09_long_sr: 31.3      # mean of 31.8/32.0\n      pi05_random_k085_long_sr: 44.3     # mean of 44.4/45.2/42.0/45.6\n      pi05_random_k07_long_sr: 66.3      # mean of 65.8/64.6/68.6\n      pi05_random_k05_long_sr: 47.6      # mean of 46.8/51.2/46.8\n      pi05_random_k03_long_sr: 28.7      # mean of 29.6/28.0/28.2/28.4\n      pi05_l2norm_k095_long_sr: 87.2     # mean of 87.0/87.4\n      pi05_l2norm_k09_long_sr: 80.3      # mean of 80.0/81.0/80.0\n      pi05_l2norm_k085_long_sr: 78.8     # mean of 78.4/79.0/78.6/77.0\n      pi05_l2norm_k07_long_sr: 63.5      # mean of 62.6/60.0/65.8/65.4\n      pi05_l2norm_k05_long_sr: 51.4      # mean of 50.2/51.4/54.0/52.6\n      pi05_l2norm_k03_long_sr: 37.5      # mean of 36.6/39.0/35.2/39.2\n\n      # Axis-2 amplification (baseline - k=0.9 random) per suite\n      axis2_amplification_object_pp: 88.0   # 98.2 - 10.2 = extreme but Object-specific cliff\n      axis2_amplification_spatial_pp: 43.2   # 97.2 - 54.0\n      axis2_amplification_goal_pp: 34.7      # 96.4 - 61.7\n      axis2_amplification_long_pp: 61.5      # 92.8 - 31.3\n\n      # Key: π0.5 Goal/Long amplification comparison\n      # π0.5 Object-to-Goal diff at k=0.9 random: 10.2→61.7 = GOAL is BETTER, not worse\n      # This means Axis-2 does NOT amplify damage for token-independent connector\n      pi05_axis2_object_vs_goal_random_k09_pp: -51.5  # Goal BETTER than Object by 51.5pp\n      pi05_axis2_object_vs_spatial_random_k09_pp: -43.8  # Spatial BETTER than Object\n\n      # CV scaling law at k=0.5 (L2norm-Random gap)\n      pi05_l2norm_random_gap_k05_object_pp: -35.4  # 33.5 - 68.9 = -35.4 (random much better)\n      pi05_l2norm_random_gap_k05_spatial_pp: -16.3  # 55.7 - 72.0 = -16.3\n      pi05_l2norm_random_gap_k05_goal_pp: -14.1     # 59.5 - 73.6 = -14.1\n      pi05_l2norm_random_gap_k05_long_pp: 3.8       # 51.4 - 47.6 = +3.8 (L2norm slightly better)\n\n      # k=0.3 reversal\n      pi05_l2norm_random_gap_k03_object_pp: 18.9  # 53.2 - 34.3 = +18.9 (L2norm wins!)\n      pi05_l2norm_random_gap_k03_spatial_pp: 6.6   # 55.0 - 48.4\n      pi05_l2norm_random_gap_k03_goal_pp: 0.1      # 51.8 - 51.7 ≈ 0\n      pi05_l2norm_random_gap_k03_long_pp: 8.8      # 37.5 - 28.7\n\n    result_rationale: >\n      Median tier 下 π0.5 数据呈现三个关键 pattern：\n\n      (1) Random cliff 是 Object-specific。Object suite 在 k=0.85-0.925 出现灾难性 dip\n      (5%→10.8%→27.6%)，但 Spatial 的 floor 保持在 54% 以上，Goal 在 k=0.9 仍有 61.7%。\n      这是因为 Object 任务需要精确的 object identity discrimination（视觉相似物体间区分），\n      而 random 在 cliff zone 恰好破坏了 concentrated critical tokens。Spatial 的关键信息\n      是分布式的（layout patches），Goal 的关键信息由 language 部分承载。\n\n      (2) Axis-2 amplification 对 π0.5 表现为 REVERSED pattern：Goal 和 Spatial 在 k=0.9\n      random 下反而 BETTER than Object（61.7% vs 10.2%）。这与 X-VLA 的 pattern 完全相反\n      （X-VLA Goal k=0.9 比 Object 差 27.8pp）。原因：token-independent connector 下，\n      pruning damage 是 local 的，不会 cascade。Object 的 cliff 是 random sampling 的\n      统计效应（concentrated critical tokens），不是 task complexity amplification。\n      因此 median tier 预测 π0.5 的 Axis-2 amplification <15pp（如果排除 Object cliff zone），\n      需要在 paper 中 qualify 2-axis framework 对 token-independent connector 的适用性。\n\n      (3) CV scaling law 在 k=0.5 成立：L2norm-random gap = -35.4pp（Object），与 CV=0.055\n      的极低值一致。但 k=0.3 出现 reversal：L2norm 反而 +18.9pp 领先。这是因为 k=0.3\n      保留 230 tokens（足够大的 budget），L2norm 的 spatial clustering 在此 budget 下\n      反而 fragment 成多个 cluster，恢复了 spatial coverage。k=0.5 是 clustering 最严重的\n      sweet spot（1 cluster, 100% concentration, 78% coverage）。\n\n    tables:\n      - caption: \"π0.5 Cross-Suite Random Pruning — Cliff Zone Comparison\"\n        columns: [\"Suite\", \"k=0.95\", \"k=0.925\", \"k=0.9\", \"k=0.85\", \"k=0.7\", \"k=0.5\", \"k=0.3\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Object\", \"72.5%\", \"28.8%\", \"10.2%\", \"4.4%\", \"75.5%\", \"68.9%\", \"34.3%\"]\n          - [\"Spatial\", \"76.6%\", \"59.3%\", \"54.0%\", \"58.8%\", \"74.1%\", \"72.0%\", \"48.4%\"]\n          - [\"Goal\", \"83.5%\", \"—\", \"61.7%\", \"52.6%\", \"76.9%\", \"73.6%\", \"51.7%\"]\n          - [\"Long\", \"62.2%\", \"—\", \"31.3%\", \"44.3%\", \"66.3%\", \"47.6%\", \"28.7%\"]\n      - caption: \"π0.5 L2norm vs Random Gap (pp) — CV Scaling Law Validation\"\n        columns: [\"Suite\", \"k=0.7\", \"k=0.5\", \"k=0.3\", \"Pattern\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Object\", \"-19.1\", \"-35.4\", \"+18.9\", \"Reversal at k=0.3\"]\n          - [\"Spatial\", \"-6.4\", \"-16.3\", \"+6.6\", \"Reversal at k=0.3\"]\n          - [\"Goal\", \"-4.9\", \"-14.1\", \"+0.1\", \"Near-zero at k=0.3\"]\n          - [\"Long\", \"-2.8\", \"+3.8\", \"+8.8\", \"L2norm consistently better\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: π0.5 random pruning cliff profile — Object (deep V-shape dip to 4.4% at k=0.85) vs Spatial (gradual, floor >54%) vs Goal/Long. Key visual: Object-specific catastrophic collapse.\"\n      - \"Fig: L2norm-Random gap vs keep ratio across 4 suites — showing k=0.5 as peak random advantage and k=0.3 reversal point.\"\n    analysis: >\n      Median tier 下需要在 paper 中加 qualification：2-axis framework 的 Axis-2 (task complexity)\n      对 token-independent connector 的 amplification effect 显著弱于 token-entangling connector。\n      π0.5 的 suite-dependent sensitivity 主要由 Object cliff（random sampling + concentrated\n      critical tokens 的统计效应）驱动，而非 task complexity amplification。\n      Claim 1 需弱化为 'connector architecture is the primary determinant; task complexity is a\n      modulating factor primarily for token-entangling connectors'。\n      CV scaling law (Claim 5) 在 k=0.5 清晰成立但 k=0.3 reversal 需要限定讨论——\n      Long suite 在所有 k 值 L2norm 都不差于 random，可能是 Long 任务的 multi-step 结构\n      使得 importance-based selection 的 token 恰好 cover 关键 subgoal transitions。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # 2. Cross-Suite Expansion (plan_id: c6_libero_suite_expansion)\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"Cross-Suite Framework Validation — 5 Models × 4 Suites\"\n    plan_id: c6_libero_suite_expansion\n    description: >\n      将 pruning 实验从 LIBERO-Object 扩展到 Spatial/Goal/Long。\n      验证 2-axis framework 跨 suite 的预测准确性。\n      Median tier 预测 framework accuracy 75-90%。\n    expected_results:\n      # X-VLA cross-suite (Axis-2 amplification — strongest evidence)\n      xvla_baseline_object: 99.2\n      xvla_baseline_spatial: 93.0\n      xvla_baseline_goal: 98.4\n      xvla_baseline_long: 94.0\n\n      xvla_l2norm_k09_object: 97.6\n      xvla_l2norm_k09_spatial: 78.8\n      xvla_l2norm_k09_goal: 70.2\n      xvla_l2norm_k09_long: 27.5\n\n      xvla_random_k09_object: 97.8\n      xvla_random_k09_spatial: 77.8\n      xvla_random_k09_goal: 70.6\n      xvla_random_k09_long: 29.6\n\n      # X-VLA Axis-2 amplification at k=0.9\n      xvla_drop_k09_object_pp: 1.6   # 99.2 - 97.6\n      xvla_drop_k09_spatial_pp: 14.2  # 93.0 - 78.8\n      xvla_drop_k09_goal_pp: 28.2     # 98.4 - 70.2\n      xvla_drop_k09_long_pp: 66.5     # 94.0 - 27.5\n\n      # X-VLA k=0.5 cross-suite — random vs l2norm\n      xvla_l2norm_k05_object: 43.4\n      xvla_random_k05_object: 70.3\n      xvla_l2norm_k05_spatial: 58.9\n      xvla_random_k05_spatial: 71.4\n      xvla_l2norm_k05_goal: 59.5\n      xvla_random_k05_goal: 67.9\n      xvla_l2norm_k05_long: 44.8\n      xvla_random_k05_long: 61.6\n\n      # SmolVLA cross-suite — all cliff-edge\n      smolvla_baseline_object: 59.2\n      smolvla_baseline_spatial: 44.6\n      smolvla_baseline_goal: 60.8\n      smolvla_baseline_long: 36.6\n      smolvla_k095_all_suites_all_methods: 0  # 0% across all suites\n\n      # Framework prediction accuracy\n      framework_correct_predictions: 17\n      framework_total_predictions: 20\n      framework_accuracy_pct: 85\n\n      # Edge cases that need qualification\n      edge_case_1: \"π0.5 Axis-2 reversed — Goal BETTER than Object at k=0.9\"\n      edge_case_2: \"X-VLA Long k=0.85 non-monotonic (35%) < k=0.5 (61.6%)\"\n      edge_case_3: \"CV scaling law k=0.3 reversal for low-CV models\"\n\n    result_rationale: >\n      Median tier framework accuracy ~85%：20 个 cross-suite predictions 中 17 个正确。\n\n      正确的 predictions：\n      - X-VLA Axis-2 amplification Object→Goal/Long（confirmed 27.8pp/66.5pp）\n      - SmolVLA all suites cliff-edge（confirmed 0% everywhere）\n      - OpenVLA graded degradation across suites\n      - CV scaling law at k=0.5（L2norm-random gap correlates with CV）\n      - L2norm plateau for π0.5 at k≥0.85 on all suites\n\n      需要 qualify 的 edge cases：\n      (1) π0.5 的 Axis-2 pattern 是 reversed（Object WORST, not Goal/Long），因为\n      token-independent connector 下 task complexity 不 amplify damage，而 Object 的\n      concentrated critical tokens 在 random cliff zone 反而最脆弱。\n      (2) X-VLA Long k=0.85 出现 non-monotonic reversal（35% < k=0.5 的 61.6%），\n      与 Object 的 non-monotonic pattern 不同——Long 的 cliff zone 在更高 k 值，\n      因为 multi-step reasoning 对 token density 的 threshold 更高。\n      (3) CV scaling law k=0.3 reversal 限制了 Claim 5 的适用范围。\n\n    tables:\n      - caption: \"2-Axis Framework — X-VLA Pruning Drop at k=0.9 Across Suites\"\n        columns: [\"Suite\", \"Baseline\", \"L2norm k=0.9\", \"Drop (pp)\", \"Axis-2 Level\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Object\", \"99.2%\", \"97.6%\", \"-1.6\", \"Simple\"]\n          - [\"Spatial\", \"93.0%\", \"78.8%\", \"-14.2\", \"Moderate\"]\n          - [\"Goal\", \"98.4%\", \"70.2%\", \"-28.2\", \"Complex\"]\n          - [\"Long\", \"94.0%\", \"27.5%\", \"-66.5\", \"Most Complex\"]\n      - caption: \"Cross-Suite L2norm vs Random Gap at k=0.5 (pp) — CV Scaling Law\"\n        columns: [\"Model\", \"CV\", \"Object\", \"Spatial\", \"Goal\", \"Long\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"pi0.5\", \"0.055\", \"-35.4\", \"-16.3\", \"-14.1\", \"+3.8\"]\n          - [\"X-VLA\", \"0.151\", \"-26.9\", \"-12.5\", \"-8.4\", \"-16.8\"]\n          - [\"OpenVLA\", \"0.215\", \"+1.8\", \"—\", \"—\", \"—\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: Heatmap of pruning drop (pp from baseline) — 5 models × 4 suites × k=0.9. Visual shows clear Axis-1 (rows) and Axis-2 (columns) gradients for X-VLA/SmolVLA, but flat for π0.5/OpenVLA across suites.\"\n    analysis: >\n      Framework accuracy 85% 落在 median tier range [75%, 90%] 中。3 个 edge cases 需要在\n      paper 中 qualify：(1) 对 π0.5 等 token-independent model，用 'connector architecture\n      determines base sensitivity; task semantics modulate through statistical token criticality\n      rather than cascading damage' 替代原先的 'task complexity amplifies'。\n      (2) X-VLA Long 的 non-monotonic pattern 需要额外 figure 说明 cliff zone 随 task\n      complexity 右移。(3) k=0.3 reversal 在 Discussion 中说明 CV scaling law 的边界条件。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # 3. VTR Cross-Suite Generalization (plan_id: c6_libero_suite_vtr)\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"VTR SmolVLA Cross-Suite Recovery (M=32 on Spatial/Goal/Long)\"\n    plan_id: c6_libero_suite_vtr\n    description: >\n      VTR M=32 在 Spatial/Goal/Long 上的 recovery 验证。\n      已有数据：M=32 Spatial=53.2%, Goal=56.4%。\n      Median tier 预测 recovery ratio 0.9-1.0。\n    expected_results:\n      # SmolVLA baselines (official checkpoint)\n      smolvla_baseline_object: 59.2\n      smolvla_baseline_spatial: 44.6\n      smolvla_baseline_goal: 60.8\n      smolvla_baseline_long: 36.6\n\n      # Hard pruning reference — all 0%\n      smolvla_prune_k05_all_suites: 0\n\n      # VTR M=32 recovery\n      vtr_m32_object_sr: 60.1        # 3-seed mean (confirmed)\n      vtr_m32_spatial_sr: 53.2       # confirmed\n      vtr_m32_goal_sr: 56.4          # confirmed\n      vtr_m32_long_sr: 35.0          # predicted: Long baseline only 36.6%, VTR recovers ~95%\n\n      # Recovery ratios\n      vtr_recovery_ratio_object: 1.015  # 60.1/59.2\n      vtr_recovery_ratio_spatial: 1.193 # 53.2/44.6 — exceeds baseline (different checkpoint)\n      vtr_recovery_ratio_goal: 0.928    # 56.4/60.8\n      vtr_recovery_ratio_long: 0.956    # 35.0/36.6\n\n      # Mean recovery ratio across suites\n      vtr_mean_recovery_ratio: 0.96\n\n      # VTR M-sweep on Object (confirmed)\n      vtr_m16_object_sr: 56.9\n      vtr_m32_object_sr_confirmed: 60.1\n      vtr_m64_object_sr: 62.0\n      vtr_m96_object_sr: 54.5\n      vtr_m128_object_sr: 58.0\n\n    result_rationale: >\n      Median tier 下 VTR 在所有 suites 都能从 0%（hard pruning）恢复到 near-baseline，\n      但 recovery ratio 有 suite-dependent variation（0.928-1.193）。\n\n      Object (recovery 1.015): VTR 在 Object 上 recovery 最稳定，因为 Object 任务的 visual\n      discriminability 需求可以被 re-encoded tokens 完整保留——pixel-shuffle 的 spatial\n      entanglement 是 Object failure 的唯一原因，VTR 修复了这个 entanglement。\n\n      Spatial (recovery 1.193): 看似超过 baseline 但需注意 baseline 是 official checkpoint\n      (44.6%) vs VTR 是 LoRA-FT + VTC (53.2%)——实际上是不同 training pipeline 的差异，\n      不应解读为 VTR 超越。Paper 中需要用 recovery from 0% 而非 absolute comparison。\n\n      Goal (recovery 0.928): 轻微低于 baseline（-4.4pp），因为 VTR 是在 Object suite 训练的，\n      Goal 的 multi-step task structure 引入了 distribution shift。Token re-encoding 恢复了\n      spatial information 但无法完全补偿 task-distribution mismatch。\n\n      Long (predicted 0.956): Long 的 baseline 最低（36.6%），VTR 的 re-encoding 在 simple\n      manipulation primitives 上有效，但 Long 需要跨多个 sub-goal 的 temporal coherence，\n      VTR 的 per-step re-encoding 无法显式捕捉 cross-step dependencies。预测 recovery ~35%，\n      略低于 baseline 但远高于 0%。\n\n      关键限定：VTR 仅对 pixel-shuffle connector 有效（OpenVLA M=128 = 0%），method\n      contribution 限于 'targeted solution for worst-case architecture'。\n\n    tables:\n      - caption: \"VTR M=32 Cross-Suite Recovery from Cliff-Edge\"\n        columns: [\"Suite\", \"Baseline\", \"Hard Prune k=0.5\", \"VTR M=32\", \"Recovery Ratio\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Object\", \"59.2%\", \"0%\", \"60.1%\", \"1.015\"]\n          - [\"Spatial\", \"44.6%*\", \"0%\", \"53.2%\", \"1.193*\"]\n          - [\"Goal\", \"60.8%\", \"0%\", \"56.4%\", \"0.928\"]\n          - [\"Long\", \"36.6%\", \"0%\", \"~35.0%\", \"~0.956\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: Bar chart — SmolVLA Baseline vs Hard Prune vs VTR M=32 across 4 suites. Visual emphasis on recovery from 0% (red) to near-baseline (green).\"\n    analysis: >\n      VTR 的 mean recovery ratio 0.96 落在 median tier range [0.9, 1.0] 中。\n      Method contribution 需明确限定为 pixel-shuffle-specific：(1) 只在 SmolVLA 上有效，\n      (2) 在非 Object suite 上有 -4.4pp 到 +8.6pp 的 variance，(3) OpenVLA VTR = 0%。\n      Paper identity 从 'analysis + method' 调整为 'primarily analysis with targeted\n      method for worst-case architecture'。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # 4. VTR on OpenVLA — Method Universality Test (plan_id: c4_ext_method_universality_openvla)\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"VTR/VTC on OpenVLA (MLP projector) — Universality Falsification\"\n    plan_id: c4_ext_method_universality_openvla\n    description: >\n      VTR M=128 已确认 0% SR（overfitting）。VTC-only M=32/M=64 training in progress。\n      Median tier 预测 VTC-only 也失败，VTR 限于 pixel-shuffle。\n    expected_results:\n      # Confirmed\n      openvla_vtr_m128_20k_sr: 0     # overfitting, identical action output\n      openvla_baseline_object_sr: 74\n\n      # Predicted VTC-only results (median tier: also fail)\n      openvla_vtc_m32_sr: 0           # predicted: same overfitting pattern\n      openvla_vtc_m64_sr: 0           # predicted: same overfitting pattern\n      openvla_vtc_m96_sr: 0           # confirmed failed training\n\n      # Training diagnostics\n      openvla_vtc_m32_train_loss: 2.5  # high, indicates poor convergence\n      openvla_vtc_m64_train_loss: 2.4\n      openvla_vtc_m96_train_loss: 2.45\n\n    result_rationale: >\n      Median tier 预测 VTC-only M=32/M=64 也会失败，原因是 MLP projector tokens 已经是\n      individually meaningful 的——re-encoding 增加了不必要的 bottleneck，导致 overfitting。\n\n      具体机制：OpenVLA 的 3-layer MLP connector 将 SigLIP features 映射为 256 个独立的\n      vision tokens，每个 token 保留了原始 spatial meaning。VTR/VTC 在这些 tokens 上\n      添加 cross-attention / MLP adapter 作为 bottleneck，但这些 tokens 不需要\n      're-encoding'——它们的 spatial information 没有被 entangle。额外的 bottleneck\n      反而限制了 information flow，导致模型 overfit 到 training set 的 action distribution。\n\n      实际 training logs 显示 M=128 在 20K steps 后 output 是 identical action（所有\n      observation 产生相同的 action sequence），这是 severe mode collapse 的 hallmark。\n      M=32/M=64 的更强 compression 会加剧而非缓解这个问题。\n\n      Training 失败的 root cause 也可能是 OpenVLA 的 7B model size 导致 VTC 的 22M params\n      相对过小（0.3% of model）——gradient signal 在 backprop 过程中被 diluted。\n\n      这个 negative result 反而 strengthens 论文：VTR 的有效性是 connector-dependent 的，\n      验证了 'connector determines both compressibility AND optimal compression strategy'。\n\n    tables:\n      - caption: \"VTR/VTC on OpenVLA vs SmolVLA — Connector-Dependent Effectiveness\"\n        columns: [\"Model\", \"Connector\", \"CV\", \"VTR M=128\", \"VTC M=32\", \"VTC M=64\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"SmolVLA\", \"Pixel-shuffle\", \"0.314\", \"58.0%\", \"60.1%\", \"62.0%\"]\n          - [\"OpenVLA\", \"3-layer MLP\", \"0.215\", \"0%\", \"~0%*\", \"~0%*\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: Training loss curves — SmolVLA VTC (converges to ~0.05) vs OpenVLA VTC (plateaus at ~2.5, fails to converge). Annotate divergence point.\"\n    analysis: >\n      VTR universality falsified。Method contribution 收窄为 pixel-shuffle-specific solution。\n      Paper 中将 VTR 定位为 'targeted re-encoding for architectures where token pruning\n      creates irreversible information loss'。Discussion 中指出 MLP projector VLAs 应\n      直接用 simple pruning（L2norm 或 random depending on CV），不需要 learned compression。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # 5. OpenVLA VTC M-Sweep (plan_id: c4_ext_openvla_msweep)\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"OpenVLA VTC M-Sweep (M=32/64/96) — Training Convergence Test\"\n    plan_id: c4_ext_openvla_msweep\n    description: >\n      OpenVLA 上 VTC-only training（不冻结 backbone），测试不同 M 值。\n      Training 已 failed/killed on all M values。\n    expected_results:\n      openvla_vtc_m32_status: \"failed\"\n      openvla_vtc_m64_status: \"failed\"\n      openvla_vtc_m96_status: \"failed\"\n      openvla_vtc_m96_final_loss: 2.45\n      openvla_vtc_m64_final_loss: null  # crashed\n      interpretation: \"VTC training does not converge on MLP-projector VLAs\"\n\n    result_rationale: >\n      All M values 的 VTC training 在 OpenVLA 上失败或 killed。M=96 跑完了 100K steps\n      但 final loss 2.45（远高于 SmolVLA 的 ~0.05），说明模型未能学到有效的 token\n      re-encoding。M=64 和 M=32 的 VTC-only training 也 crashed/failed。\n\n      Root cause：OpenVLA (7B) 是 frozen backbone + 22M compressor 的极端不平衡。\n      SmolVLA (450M) 的 compressor/backbone ratio = 22M/450M = 4.9%，而 OpenVLA 的\n      ratio = 22M/7B = 0.3%。VTC 的 gradient signal 在通过 7B frozen backbone 的\n      attention layers 时被严重 attenuate，导致 compressor 无法学到有用的 representation。\n\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      OpenVLA VTC M-sweep 的 universal failure 进一步确认 VTR/VTC 仅对 pixel-shuffle\n      connector 有效。Paper 中在 Table 5 或 supplementary 中报告这些 negative results，\n      强化 'VTR effectiveness is connector-dependent' 的 claim。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # 6. OFT Graded Degradation (plan_id: c3_oft_graded_full)\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"OpenVLA-OFT Cross-Suite Pruning (Blocked by GPU Incompatibility)\"\n    plan_id: c3_oft_graded_full\n    description: >\n      OFT (7B, 3-layer MLP, DINOv2+SigLIP fused, 512 tokens) 在 4 suites 上的\n      baseline + pruning。Blocked by Blackwell GPU SDPA incompatibility。\n      Median tier 用 CV/entropy analysis 替代 SR eval。\n    expected_results:\n      # Confirmed diagnostic metrics\n      oft_cv: 0.219\n      oft_entropy: 0.667\n      oft_tokens: 512\n      oft_baseline_official_sr: 97  # cited from original paper\n\n      # Predicted pruning behavior (from CV analogy with OpenVLA CV=0.215)\n      oft_predicted_k09_sr: 65    # slightly worse than OpenVLA (62%) due to 512 tokens\n      oft_predicted_k07_sr: 50\n      oft_predicted_k05_sr: 38\n      oft_predicted_k03_sr: 22\n\n      # L2norm vs random gap (predicted from CV=0.219 ≈ OpenVLA)\n      oft_l2norm_random_gap_k05_pp: -2  # near-zero, consistent with high-CV pattern\n      oft_l2norm_advantage_mild_k: true  # L2norm slightly better at k≥0.7\n\n      # Why we can't run this\n      blocker: \"Blackwell GPU SDPA incompatibility — requires A100 + torch 2.2\"\n\n    result_rationale: >\n      OFT eval 被 Blackwell GPU 的 SDPA 不兼容 blocked。Median tier 下仅用 diagnostic\n      metrics 参与分析：CV=0.219 ≈ OpenVLA (0.215)，entropy=0.667 ≈ OpenVLA (0.661)。\n      \n      这两个 near-identical diagnostic values 预测 OFT 的 pruning behavior 与 OpenVLA\n      几乎一致——graded degradation，L2norm 在 aggressive k 略优于 random。\n      512 tokens (vs OpenVLA 的 256) 意味着 absolute token budget 在 same k ratio 下\n      更大（k=0.5 保留 256 vs 128），可能导致略好的 SR，但 degradation PATTERN 应相同。\n\n      关键 paper value：OFT 用了不同的 action head（Optimal Flow Transport vs standard），\n      但 CV 和 entropy 几乎 identical → 确认 connector（not action head）determines\n      attention structure 和 pruning behavior。这是一个 clean controlled comparison。\n\n      Median tier 下 OFT 作为 supplementary evidence 出现（CV/entropy table），\n      不作为 primary experimental evidence。Cite official baseline ~97%，\n      acknowledge eval 未能完成。\n\n    tables:\n      - caption: \"Connector vs Action Head — Diagnostic Decoupling\"\n        columns: [\"Model\", \"Action Head\", \"Connector\", \"CV\", \"Entropy\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"OpenVLA\", \"Standard (MLP)\", \"3-layer MLP\", \"0.215\", \"0.661\"]\n          - [\"OpenVLA-OFT\", \"OFT (flow)\", \"3-layer MLP\", \"0.219\", \"0.667\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: Scatter plot of CV vs Entropy for all 6 models — OFT and OpenVLA as overlapping points, confirming connector-dominance over action-head.\"\n    analysis: >\n      OFT 贡献收窄为 diagnostic decoupling evidence。Paper 中用一句话总结：\n      'OFT (CV=0.219) ≈ Standard OpenVLA (CV=0.215) despite different action heads,\n      confirming that connector architecture, not downstream components, determines\n      token importance distribution.' Eval SR 不可得，acknowledged as limitation。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # 7. OFT CV Diagnostic (plan_id: diagnostic_oft_cv)\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"OFT Token Importance CV Measurement\"\n    plan_id: diagnostic_oft_cv\n    description: >\n      OFT importance CV 测量，完成 6-model diagnostic table 的最后一个空位。\n    expected_results:\n      oft_importance_cv: 0.219\n      oft_importance_cv_std: 0.012\n      oft_importance_gini: 0.11\n      oft_n_tokens: 512\n      spectrum_position: \"between OpenVLA (0.215) and SmolVLA (0.314)\"\n\n    result_rationale: >\n      OFT 使用与 OpenVLA 相同的 3-layer MLP connector（GELU activation），唯一差异是\n      (1) fused DINOv2+SigLIP encoder 产生 512 tokens（vs OpenVLA 的 256），\n      (2) OFT action head。Entropy 已确认 0.667 ≈ 0.661，CV 预测 0.219 ≈ 0.215。\n      微小的 CV 差异（+0.004）可能来自 DINOv2 features 的 additional modality 引入的\n      slightly higher token heterogeneity。\n\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      CV=0.219 完成 6-model spectrum：π0(0.038) < π0.5(0.055) < X-VLA(0.151) <\n      OpenVLA(0.215) ≈ OFT(0.219) < SmolVLA(0.314)。\n      Paper Table 1 中 OFT 行填入 CV=0.219, Entropy=0.667, Pruning='Graded (predicted)'。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # 8. X-VLA Cliff Localization (plan_id: c1_xvla_threshold_localization)\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"X-VLA k=0.8/k=0.85 3-Seed Cliff Localization\"\n    plan_id: c1_xvla_threshold_localization\n    description: >\n      X-VLA Object cliff threshold 精确定位：k=0.85 (67.9% ± 0.31pp, 3-seed) 和\n      k=0.80 (89.0% ± 0.72pp, 3-seed)。Non-monotonic: k=0.85 < k=0.80。\n    expected_results:\n      # L2norm 3-seed\n      xvla_l2norm_k085_object_mean: 67.9\n      xvla_l2norm_k085_object_std: 0.31\n      xvla_l2norm_k085_seeds: [68.0, 67.6, 68.2]\n      xvla_l2norm_k080_object_mean: 89.0\n      xvla_l2norm_k080_object_std: 0.72\n      xvla_l2norm_k080_seeds: [88.8, 88.4, 89.8]\n\n      # Random comparison\n      xvla_random_k085_object_mean: 64.3\n      xvla_random_k085_seeds: [65.0, 63.6, 63.2]\n      xvla_random_k080_object_mean: 89.4\n      xvla_random_k080_seeds: [89.4]\n\n      # Non-monotonicity\n      non_monotonic_gap_pp: 21.1  # k=0.80 - k=0.85 = 89.0 - 67.9\n      cliff_width_k_units: 0.05   # from k=0.85 (cliff) to k=0.80 (recovery)\n\n      # Cross-method consistency\n      l2norm_random_k085_gap_pp: 3.6  # L2norm slightly better (67.9 vs 64.3)\n      both_crash_same_tasks: true     # T1, T4, T6, T8 crash for both methods\n\n    result_rationale: >\n      3-seed deterministic data 确认 cliff 位于 k=0.85（42 tokens kept），且\n      k=0.80（40 tokens）recovery 到 89%——仅差 2 个 tokens 但 21pp gap。\n\n      Non-monotonicity 来自 BART encoder 的 length-dependent interactions：\n      - k=0.85 (42 tokens): BART 的 12-layer self-attention 在 42 tokens 上产生\n        destructive interference pattern——刚好是 critical token density threshold\n      - k=0.80 (40 tokens): 少保留 2 个 tokens 反而破坏了这个 interference pattern，\n        恢复了正常的 information flow\n\n      SD < 1pp across all 3 seeds 确认 cliff 是完全 deterministic 的（L2norm pruning\n      是 deterministic function of token norms），不是 stochastic noise。\n\n      L2norm 和 random 在 cliff zone 都 crash on same 4 tasks (T1=cream_cheese,\n      T4=ketchup, T6=butter, T8=chocolate_pudding) → cliff 是 architectural，\n      不是 method-specific。\n\n    tables:\n      - caption: \"X-VLA Object Cliff Zone — 3-Seed Deterministic (L2norm)\"\n        columns: [\"k\", \"Tokens Kept\", \"Seed 42\", \"Seed 43\", \"Seed 44\", \"Mean\", \"SD\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"0.90\", \"45\", \"97.6%\", \"—\", \"98.2%\", \"97.6%\", \"—\"]\n          - [\"0.85\", \"42\", \"68.0%\", \"67.6%\", \"68.2%\", \"67.9%\", \"0.31\"]\n          - [\"0.80\", \"40\", \"88.8%\", \"88.4%\", \"89.8%\", \"89.0%\", \"0.72\"]\n          - [\"0.70\", \"35\", \"56.2%\", \"59.0%\", \"56.4%\", \"57.2%\", \"1.56\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: X-VLA Object cliff profile with 3-seed error bars — sharp V-shape at k=0.85, recovery at k=0.80. Annotate '2 tokens, 21pp gap'.\"\n    analysis: >\n      Cliff localization 完成。Paper 中用 1 figure 展示 X-VLA 的 full pruning curve\n      (k=0.1 to k=0.95)，annotate k=0.85 cliff 和 non-monotonic recovery。\n      Discussion 中说明 BART encoder 的 length-dependent interaction 机制。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # 9. Perceiver Resampler — 3rd Connector Family (plan_id: c5_third_connector_roboflamingo)\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"RoboFlamingo Perceiver Resampler Fine-tune + Pruning\"\n    plan_id: c5_third_connector_roboflamingo\n    description: >\n      Perceiver Resampler connector 作为第 3 个 connector family 验证。\n      Training killed twice。Median tier 预测即使完成也不会改变核心结论。\n    expected_results:\n      # Training status\n      training_status: \"killed\"\n      training_attempts: 2\n\n      # Predicted results IF training succeeded\n      roboflamingo_predicted_cv: 0.18     # between X-VLA (0.151) and OpenVLA (0.215)\n      roboflamingo_predicted_entropy: 0.72\n      roboflamingo_predicted_baseline_sr: 55  # lower baseline due to smaller model\n      roboflamingo_predicted_k09_sr: 48       # moderate degradation\n      roboflamingo_predicted_k05_sr: 28       # significant degradation\n\n      # Paper impact\n      would_strengthen_paper: false   # marginal value — already have 5 models\n      paper_coverage_without: \"5 models × 3 families sufficient for CoRL\"\n\n    result_rationale: >\n      RoboFlamingo training 两次 killed，likely due to (1) Perceiver Resampler 与 LIBERO\n      task distribution 的 incompatibility，(2) fine-tuning instability from frozen\n      cross-attention + trainable resampler 的 gradient mismatch。\n\n      即使完成，Perceiver Resampler 的预测 CV=0.18 会落在 X-VLA 和 OpenVLA 之间——\n      介于 token-entangling 和 token-independent 之间。这不会改变 2-axis framework\n      的核心结论，只是增加一个中间数据点。\n\n      Median tier 下 5 models × 3 families (linear / MLP / pixel-shuffle) 已经足够\n      支撑 CoRL submission。Perceiver Resampler 作为 'future work' 提及。\n\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      Dropped from paper scope。在 Discussion 中提到 'additional connector families\n      (e.g., Perceiver Resampler, cross-attention based) remain to be validated'\n      作为 limitation 和 future direction。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # 10. E5 Attention Pruning — Additional Method (cross-cutting)\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"E5 Attention-Based Pruning — X-VLA vs π0.5 Cross-Suite\"\n    plan_id: c6_libero_suite_expansion\n    description: >\n      Attention-based pruning (E5) 在 X-VLA 和 π0.5 上的 cross-suite 结果。\n      X-VLA attention pruning 表现极好（Object 99.2%, Long 90.2%），\n      π0.5 attention 在 Object k=0.7 catastrophic (0.6%) 但 Goal 70.2%。\n      Median tier：Goal 初始 0% 后修复为 98.2%，需额外 seed 确认可靠性。\n    expected_results:\n      # X-VLA E5 attention pruning (confirmed — near-lossless)\n      xvla_attn_last_k05_object: 99.2\n      xvla_attn_mean_k05_object: 98.4\n      xvla_attn_rollout_k05_object: 97.4\n      xvla_attn_last_k05_spatial: 88.8\n      xvla_attn_mean_k05_spatial: 91.6\n      xvla_attn_rollout_k05_spatial: 92.8\n      xvla_attn_last_k05_goal: 98.2   # AFTER fix (was 0% before fix)\n      xvla_attn_mean_k05_goal: 97.4\n      xvla_attn_rollout_k05_goal: 96.8\n      xvla_attn_last_k05_long: 90.2\n      xvla_attn_mean_k05_long: 94.0\n      xvla_attn_rollout_k05_long: 94.8\n\n      # X-VLA attention k=0.3 (more aggressive)\n      xvla_attn_last_k03_object: 84.2\n      xvla_attn_mean_k03_object: 96.0\n      xvla_attn_mean_k03_spatial: 90.4\n      xvla_attn_last_k03_spatial: 85.6\n\n      # π0.5 E5 attention pruning (mixed results)\n      pi05_attn_k095_object: 98.4    # near-lossless at mild compression\n      pi05_attn_k09_object: 97.2     # still good\n      pi05_attn_k085_object: 92.2    # starts degrading\n      pi05_attn_k07_object: 0.6      # CATASTROPHIC — attention becomes adversarial\n      pi05_attn_k05_object: 37.8     # partial recovery\n      pi05_attn_k05_spatial: 72.6    # spatial robust\n      pi05_attn_k05_goal: 71.2       # mean of 70.2/72.2\n      pi05_attn_k05_long: 49.4\n\n      # OpenVLA attention pruning\n      openvla_attn_k09_object: 61.4\n      openvla_attn_k085_object: 55.0\n      openvla_attn_k09_goal: 73.2\n      openvla_attn_k09_spatial: 80.4\n\n      # Goal fix reliability\n      xvla_attn_goal_fix_needed: true\n      xvla_attn_goal_seed42_sr: 98.2\n      xvla_attn_goal_seed43_needed: true  # additional seed for confirmation\n      xvla_attn_goal_predicted_seed43_sr: 97.5  # predicted: fix is genuine\n\n    result_rationale: >\n      E5 attention pruning 在不同 model 上表现 divergent：\n\n      X-VLA (BART encoder)：attention pruning 近乎 lossless，因为 BART 的 12-layer\n      self-attention 产生了 meaningful attention patterns——high-attention tokens 确实\n      是最重要的。k=0.5 Object 99.2% vs L2norm 42.6% → attention 比 L2norm 好 56.6pp。\n      这是因为 BART encoder 的 attention 直接反映了 token 间的 functional dependency。\n\n      Goal suite 初始为 0%（bug），修复后 98.2% → 需要 seed43 确认 fix 是 genuine。\n      Median tier 预测 seed43 = 97.5%（fix 是 valid 的，但需要额外 seed 才能在\n      paper 中 claim）。\n\n      π0.5 (linear projection)：attention pruning 在 k=0.7 catastrophic (0.6%)，\n      因为 PaliGemma 的 per-layer attention 在中间 k 值产生了 adversarial selection。\n      π0.5 的 attention entropy = 0.666，说明 attention 分布有 moderate sharpness，\n      但不 correlate with true token importance（CV=0.055 说明所有 tokens equally\n      important）。Attention-based pruning 在 uniform-importance model 上不可靠。\n\n      OpenVLA (MLP)：attention pruning k=0.9 Object = 61.4% < L2norm = 70.6% < random = 69.2%。\n      Attention 是三种方法中最差的，因为 MLP connector 后的 attention 也不 reliable\n      predict token importance。\n\n      Paper value：attention pruning 的 effectiveness 也是 connector-dependent，\n      strengthening 'connector determines optimal compression strategy' claim。\n\n    tables:\n      - caption: \"E5 Attention Pruning k=0.5 — Cross-Model Cross-Suite\"\n        columns: [\"Model\", \"Object\", \"Spatial\", \"Goal\", \"Long\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"X-VLA (attn-last)\", \"99.2%\", \"88.8%\", \"98.2%*\", \"90.2%\"]\n          - [\"X-VLA (attn-mean)\", \"98.4%\", \"91.6%\", \"97.4%\", \"94.0%\"]\n          - [\"pi0.5 (attn)\", \"37.8%\", \"72.6%\", \"71.2%\", \"49.4%\"]\n          - [\"X-VLA (L2norm)\", \"42.6%\", \"58.8%\", \"59.0%\", \"44.6%\"]\n          - [\"X-VLA (random)\", \"70.6%\", \"71.4%\", \"67.9%\", \"61.6%\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: Method comparison radar chart — X-VLA at k=0.5: attention (near-lossless) vs L2norm (42.6%) vs random (70.6%) across 4 suites. Shows attention dominance for BART connector.\"\n    analysis: >\n      E5 attention pruning 提供了 Claim 5 的重要扩展：不只是 L2norm vs random 的\n      strategy depends on CV，attention-based methods 也是 connector-dependent。\n      BART connector 的 attention 是 reliable signal（因为 12-layer self-attention\n      creates meaningful importance distribution），而 linear/MLP connector 的 attention\n      不可靠。Paper 中可以加一行 Table showing method effectiveness rank per model。\n      但 Goal 0%→98.2% 的 fix 需要 seed43 确认，Median tier 下这个 reliability concern\n      需要在 paper 中 transparent disclosure。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # 11. CV Scaling Law Consolidation (cross-cutting analysis)\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"CV Scaling Law — Spearman Correlation Across Conditions\"\n    plan_id: c6_libero_suite_expansion\n    description: >\n      CV 作为 pruning strategy predictor 的 Spearman correlation 分析。\n      Median tier 预测 abs(Spearman) 在 0.6-0.85 之间。\n    expected_results:\n      # k=0.5 scaling law (strongest)\n      cv_vs_l2norm_random_gap_k05_spearman: 0.82\n      cv_vs_l2norm_random_gap_k05_p_value: 0.03\n\n      # k=0.7 scaling law (confirmatory)\n      cv_vs_l2norm_random_gap_k07_spearman: 0.75\n      cv_vs_l2norm_random_gap_k07_p_value: 0.05\n\n      # k=0.3 scaling law (REVERSED for low-CV)\n      cv_vs_l2norm_random_gap_k03_spearman: 0.45   # weak — reversal breaks monotonicity\n      cv_vs_l2norm_random_gap_k03_p_value: 0.15    # not significant\n\n      # Cross-suite Spearman (averaging across suites)\n      cv_strategy_abs_spearman_mean: 0.74   # within [0.6, 0.85] range\n\n      # Data points used\n      n_models_k05: 3   # π0.5 (0.055), X-VLA (0.151), OpenVLA (0.215)\n      n_suites_k05: 1   # Object only for 3-model comparison\n      datapoints_k05:\n        - {model: \"pi0.5\", cv: 0.055, gap_pp: -35.4}\n        - {model: \"X-VLA\", cv: 0.151, gap_pp: -26.9}\n        - {model: \"OpenVLA\", cv: 0.215, gap_pp: 1.8}\n\n      # k=0.5 validated at two k values\n      k05_gap_monotonic: true    # -35.4 → -26.9 → +1.8\n      k07_gap_monotonic: true    # -22.2 → -6.5 → +5.4\n      k03_gap_monotonic: false   # +18.9 → -42.3 → -3.6 — NOT monotonic\n\n    result_rationale: >\n      CV scaling law 的 Spearman correlation 0.74 落在 median tier range [0.6, 0.85] 中。\n\n      k=0.5 是最 clean 的 scaling law validation point：3 个 model 的 L2norm-random gap\n      与 CV 呈单调关系（-35.4pp → -26.9pp → +1.8pp as CV increases 0.055 → 0.151 → 0.215）。\n      Spearman = 0.82，因为只有 3 个 data points 所以 p-value 边缘显著。\n\n      k=0.7 作为 confirmatory second row：pattern 一致但 gap magnitudes 小（-22.2 → -6.5 → +5.4），\n      Spearman = 0.75。\n\n      k=0.3 BREAKS the scaling law：π0.5 reversal (+18.9pp L2norm wins) 但 X-VLA\n      random 仍大幅领先 (+42.3pp)。这不是 CV 不好，而是 absolute token budget 的交互效应：\n      π0.5 k=0.3 保留 230 tokens（大 budget），X-VLA k=0.3 保留 15 tokens（小 budget）。\n      Large budget + low CV = L2norm 可以 fragment clusters 恢复 diversity。\n      Small budget + mid CV = 无论如何都太少，random 保持 stochastic diversity 的优势。\n\n      Paper strategy：k=0.5 作为 main table，k=0.7 作为 confirmatory。k=0.3 reversal\n      在 Discussion 中说明，强调 'CV predicts strategy preference at moderate compression\n      (k=0.5-0.7); at extreme compression (k=0.3), absolute token budget introduces\n      additional interaction'。Claim 5 加限定 'at moderate compression'。\n\n    tables:\n      - caption: \"CV Scaling Law — L2norm vs Random Gap (pp) at k=0.5 and k=0.7\"\n        columns: [\"Model\", \"CV\", \"Gap k=0.7 (pp)\", \"Gap k=0.5 (pp)\", \"Gap k=0.3 (pp)\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"pi0.5\", \"0.055\", \"-22.2\", \"-35.4\", \"+18.9\"]\n          - [\"X-VLA\", \"0.151\", \"-6.5\", \"-26.9\", \"-42.3\"]\n          - [\"OpenVLA\", \"0.215\", \"+5.4\", \"+1.8\", \"+3.6\"]\n      - caption: \"Spearman Correlation: CV vs Strategy Gap\"\n        columns: [\"k value\", \"Spearman rho\", \"p-value\", \"Monotonic?\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"0.7\", \"0.75\", \"0.05\", \"Yes\"]\n          - [\"0.5\", \"0.82\", \"0.03\", \"Yes\"]\n          - [\"0.3\", \"0.45\", \"0.15\", \"No (reversal)\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: Scatter plot with regression line — CV (x-axis) vs L2norm-Random gap (y-axis) at k=0.5. Three points with clear positive trend. Annotate Spearman=0.82.\"\n    analysis: >\n      Claim 5 survives review but需要加限定。原 claim 'CV predicts optimal pruning strategy'\n      改为 'CV predicts optimal pruning strategy at moderate compression (k=0.5-0.7)'。\n      k=0.3 reversal 说明 strategy preference = f(CV, k, absolute_token_budget)，\n      不是仅 CV 决定。这个 nuance 在 median tier 下是可以接受的——reviewers 会 appreciate\n      honest boundary conditions。3-4 个 claims survive review 的预测中，这个 claim\n      以 qualified form survive。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # 12. SmolVLA VTR Learned Re-encoding Consolidation (plan_id: c4_learned_reencoding_smolvla)\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"SmolVLA VTR M-Sweep 3-Seed Consolidation + Architecture Control\"\n    plan_id: c4_learned_reencoding_smolvla\n    description: >\n      VTR M-sweep (M=16/32/64/96/128) 的 3-seed 最终结果 + MLP adapter 对照。\n      已有大量数据，Median tier 下 consolidate 最终 statistics。\n    expected_results:\n      # 3-seed M-sweep (cross-attention VTC)\n      vtr_m16_3seed_mean: 56.9\n      vtr_m16_3seed_std: 1.3\n      vtr_m16_3seed_seeds: [55.8, 58.4, 56.5]\n\n      vtr_m32_3seed_mean: 60.1\n      vtr_m32_3seed_std: 1.3\n      vtr_m32_3seed_seeds: [61.6, 59.2, 59.6]\n\n      vtr_m64_3seed_mean: 62.0\n      vtr_m64_3seed_std: 2.3\n      vtr_m64_3seed_seeds: [61.6, 60.0, 64.4]\n\n      vtr_m96_3seed_mean: 54.5\n      vtr_m96_3seed_std: 3.2\n      vtr_m96_3seed_seeds: [52.6, 58.2, 52.8]\n\n      vtr_m128_3seed_mean: 58.0\n      vtr_m128_3seed_std: 3.5\n      vtr_m128_3seed_seeds: [59.8, 54.0, 60.2]\n\n      # M-curve flatness\n      m_curve_range_pp: 7.5           # max(62.0) - min(54.5)\n      m_curve_vs_baseline_max_diff: 5.3  # max deviation from baseline 59.2%\n      m_curve_flat: true\n\n      # MLP adapter control (3-seed)\n      mlp_adapter_m32_3seed_mean: 63.4\n      mlp_adapter_m32_3seed_std: 2.6\n      mlp_adapter_m32_3seed_seeds: [65.2, 64.6, 60.4]\n\n      # Architecture independence t-test\n      vtc_vs_mlp_t_stat: 1.94\n      vtc_vs_mlp_p_value: 0.15\n      architecture_independent: true\n\n      # Baseline comparison\n      smolvla_baseline: 59.2\n      hard_prune_k05: 0\n      recovery_from_zero: true\n\n    result_rationale: >\n      VTR M-sweep 确认 M-curve 是 flat 的：M=16 (56.9%) 到 M=128 (58.0%)，\n      all within ±5pp of baseline 59.2%。这意味着 VTR 对 pixel-shuffle connector\n      实现了 near-lossless compression at ANY ratio (0-87.5%)。\n\n      M=64 是 absolute best (62.0%)，M=96 是 lowest (54.5%) 但 p=0.034 与 M=64\n      的差异 statistically significant——M=96 的 higher variance (3.2pp) 和 lower mean\n      可能是因为 96-token representation 落在 an awkward regime：不够多以 passthrough\n      (M=128)，但 compression ratio 不够大 to force useful abstraction (M=32/64)。\n\n      MLP adapter (63.4%) vs VTC (60.1%) p=0.15 → architecture independent。\n      任何 learned re-encoding 都能从 0% 恢复到 baseline。\n\n      Median tier 下 VTR 的 contribution statement 明确：'VTR achieves near-lossless\n      compression at any ratio for pixel-shuffle connectors, recovering from 0%\n      (hard pruning) to ~59% (baseline)'。不 overclaim 超过 baseline。\n\n    tables:\n      - caption: \"VTR M-Sweep — 3-Seed Statistics (SmolVLA Object)\"\n        columns: [\"M\", \"Compression\", \"Mean SR (%)\", \"Std (pp)\", \"vs Baseline\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"16\", \"87.5%\", \"56.9\", \"1.3\", \"-2.3pp\"]\n          - [\"32\", \"75.0%\", \"60.1\", \"1.3\", \"+0.9pp\"]\n          - [\"64\", \"50.0%\", \"62.0\", \"2.3\", \"+2.8pp\"]\n          - [\"96\", \"25.0%\", \"54.5\", \"3.2\", \"-4.7pp\"]\n          - [\"128\", \"0% (pass)\", \"58.0\", \"3.5\", \"-1.2pp\"]\n          - [\"MLP-32\", \"75.0%\", \"63.4\", \"2.6\", \"+4.2pp\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: M-curve with error bars — flat profile, all within baseline ±5pp band (shaded). Hard prune reference at 0%.\"\n    analysis: >\n      VTR results 完备。Paper 中用 M-curve figure + architecture control table\n      支撑 Claim 4。Key limitation：仅对 pixel-shuffle 有效（OpenVLA 0%），\n      method contribution 限于 worst-case architecture。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # 13. Claims Survival Analysis — Median Tier\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"Claims Survival Under Review — Median Tier Assessment\"\n    plan_id: c6_libero_suite_expansion\n    description: >\n      5 个 core claims 在 median tier 下的 review survival 预测。\n      预测 3-4 个 claims survive。\n    expected_results:\n      claims_surviving: 3.5  # 3 full + 1 qualified\n\n      claim_1_2axis_framework:\n        status: \"survives with qualification\"\n        original: \"governed by two axes\"\n        revised: \"primarily explained by connector architecture, with task complexity as a modulating factor for token-entangling connectors\"\n        qualification: \"Axis-2 amplification weak for token-independent connectors (π0.5)\"\n        strength: 0.8\n\n      claim_2_pixel_shuffle_entanglement:\n        status: \"survives fully\"\n        evidence: \"7 conditions × 4 suites × official checkpoint → 0%\"\n        strength: 1.0\n\n      claim_3_graded_degradation:\n        status: \"survives fully\"\n        evidence: \"OpenVLA 6-point curve + OFT CV/entropy confirmation\"\n        strength: 0.95\n\n      claim_4_vtr_recovery:\n        status: \"survives with limitation\"\n        original: \"universal compression via VTR\"\n        revised: \"VTR recovers pixel-shuffle from 0% to baseline; ineffective for MLP projector\"\n        limitation: \"method contribution narrowed to pixel-shuffle-specific\"\n        strength: 0.7\n\n      claim_5_cv_scaling_law:\n        status: \"survives with boundary condition\"\n        original: \"CV predicts optimal strategy\"\n        revised: \"CV predicts optimal strategy at moderate compression (k=0.5-0.7)\"\n        boundary: \"k=0.3 reversal for low-CV models with large token budgets\"\n        strength: 0.75\n\n    result_rationale: >\n      Median tier 预测 3.5 claims survive（3 full + 1.5 qualified），落在 [3, 4] range。\n\n      Claim 2（pixel-shuffle entanglement）是最 robust 的——0% at k=0.95, all methods,\n      all suites, official checkpoint, dual-seed confirmed。没有任何 edge case。\n\n      Claim 3（graded degradation）也 robust——OpenVLA 6-point curve 是 clean monotonic，\n      OFT CV/entropy confirmation 是 clean controlled comparison。\n\n      Claim 1（2-axis framework）需要 qualification 因为 Axis-2 对 token-independent\n      connectors 的 amplification 弱于预期。Paper 不能说 'task complexity always amplifies\n      pruning sensitivity'，而是 'task complexity amplifies sensitivity SPECIFICALLY for\n      token-entangling connectors where pruning damage cascades'。\n\n      Claim 4（VTR）的 method contribution 收窄——OpenVLA 0% 意味着 VTR 不是 universal。\n      Reviewers 可能 question: 'if VTR only works on pixel-shuffle, and pixel-shuffle is\n      the architecture you're warning against, isn't the method contribution circular?'\n      Response: 'VTR provides a migration path for existing pixel-shuffle VLAs, not a\n      design recommendation for new ones.'\n\n      Claim 5（CV scaling law）加 boundary condition 后仍有价值——k=0.5-0.7 的 scaling law\n      是 clean 的（Spearman 0.75-0.82），只是 k=0.3 有 reversal。\n\n    tables:\n      - caption: \"Claims Survival Assessment — Median Tier\"\n        columns: [\"Claim\", \"Original Strength\", \"Median Tier Status\", \"Revised Strength\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"C1: 2-Axis Framework\", \"Strong\", \"Qualified\", \"0.80\"]\n          - [\"C2: Pixel-Shuffle\", \"Strong\", \"Fully Survives\", \"1.00\"]\n          - [\"C3: Graded Degradation\", \"Strong\", \"Fully Survives\", \"0.95\"]\n          - [\"C4: VTR Recovery\", \"Moderate\", \"Limited to pixel-shuffle\", \"0.70\"]\n          - [\"C5: CV Scaling Law\", \"Moderate\", \"Boundary at k=0.3\", \"0.75\"]\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      Paper identity 调整为 'primarily analysis with targeted method'。\n      Title 改为 'How Vision Connectors Shape Token Pruning Robustness in VLAs'——\n      更保守但准确。Contribution statement 聚焦：(1) first systematic cross-architecture\n      token pruning analysis in VLAs (5 models × 4 suites), (2) CV as zero-cost\n      diagnostic for pruning tolerance AND strategy, (3) VTR as targeted recovery\n      method for worst-case (pixel-shuffle) connectors。仍提交 CoRL。\n```","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"f3a93c25-07a2-42fa-8e9c-436d384627d6","total_cost_usd":1.68151725,"usage":{"input_tokens":5,"cache_creation_input_tokens":118627,"cache_read_input_tokens":380697,"output_tokens":25977,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":118627,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":25583,"cache_read_input_tokens":130289,"cache_creation_input_tokens":179,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":179},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":100170,"outputTokens":26,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.1003,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000},"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":5,"outputTokens":25977,"cacheReadInputTokens":380697,"cacheCreationInputTokens":118627,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":1.58121725,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"28111a7f-fdd2-4388-ba30-9df1104d4e82"}
